\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar remains strong, more inflows seen.   \b0\par\par\uc2 751 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Dezember 2003\par 10:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Dec 31 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar remained\par stubbornly strong against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday,\par shrugging off repeated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) to weaken it as money for investment flows in.\par     Dealers expect the local unit to hold above its pegged\par exchange rate of 7.80 to the dollar for at least a couple of\par months.\par     "I think some investors are shunning U.S.-denominated assets\par because the greenback is weak, but they need to find a way out\par for their ample funds," one trader at a local bank said.\par     "Investors have fixed their eyes on the Hong Kong equities\par market and that's why liquidity keeps streaming into the city,"\par the trader said.\par     The greenback slipped to a fresh record low against the euro\par on Wednesday and fell against the Japanese yen. The Hong Kong\par dollar rose along with other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The HKMA, the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par for the sixth time in two days on Wednesday afternoon in a bid to\par rein in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength.\par     It sold a total of HK$2.337 billion and bought U.S. dollars\par in two separate moves on Wednesday in addition to selling\par HK$1.227 billion (US$158 million) on Tuesday.\par     The latest move will further boost the aggregate balance -- a\par key measure of interbank liquidity -- to a new high of HK$31.841\par billion on Monday.\par     After the latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar exchange\par rate  was trading at 7.7630/35 at 0811 GMT, only marginally\par weaker than 7.7630/31 at mid-morning. It has appreciated by about\par 0.46 percent compared with around 7.7988 last year.\par     The local unit strengthened sharply in late September to\par 7.705, driven by speculation about a revaluation of the Chinese\par yuan, brighter domestic economic prospects, and capital inflows.\par     It has slowly retreated to the 7.76-7.77 level after numerous\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the HKMA, which has sold a cumulative HK$31.336\par billion since September.\par  \par     The HKMA has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at around 7.7630 recently and dealers\par saw that as a support level for the U.S. dollar.\par     Some dealers said strong gains in the Hong Kong stock market\par and a flurry of high profile initial public offerings have\par fuelled an inflow of funds and demand for the local dollar.\par     Hong Kong stocks ended modestly higher on the final trading\par day of 2003 on Wednesday, capping a solid 35 percent gain for the\par year that snapped a three-year losing streak.\par     Traders see a risk of further HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the near\par term as a number of Chinese firms will seek listings in Hong Kong\par next year that will attract more overseas investors.\par     Auditing firm PricewaterhouseCoopers predicted funds raised\par from Hong Kong IPOs could reach HK$100 billion (US$12.8 billion)\par next year.\par     "If the stock market continues to rise, the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is\par to remain comparatively strong," said a dealer at a Japanese\par bank.\par     Another dealer from a European bank expects the Hong Kong\par dollar to remain strong for at least three to six months.\par     Hong Kong interbank interest rates fell in the face of\par capital inflows and the rises in interbank liquidity. Short-term\par rates traded near zero.\par     The discount on the one-year Hong Kong dollar forwards\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 , reflecting the market perceptions of the unit's   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 appreciation over the next year, widened to a new low 610/590   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 pips from Tuesday's close of 575/555 pips.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A pip represents 1/10,000 of a Hong Kong dollar.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong financial markets will be closed on Thursday for   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Year's Day and reopen on Friday.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0850 GMT   At 0345 GMT   At 0900 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7630/33     7.7630/31     7.7631/32\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -195 / -190   -192 / -185   -188 / -183\par     Six-month        -375 / -355   -365 / -355   -360 / -350\par     One-year         -610 / -590   -590 / -570   -575 / -555\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight        0.005/0.008 0.0005 / 0.001 0.002 / 0.005\par     Three-month      0.06 / 0.08   0.07 / 0.08   0.09 / 0.10\par     Six-month        0.17 / 0.19   0.18 / 0.20   0.20 / 0.21\par     One-year         0.58 / 0.60   0.60 / 0.63   0.61 / 0.63\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031231dzcv002ym\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\pi