\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar remains strong despite HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Dezember 2003\par 05:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Dec 31 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the fifth time in two days on Wednesday\par morning to try to stabilise the territory's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but it\par remained stubbornly strong against the U.S. dollar, to which it\par is pegged.\par     The HKMA sold HK$1.009 billion and bought U.S. dollars, in\par the latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  late on Wednesday morning. It sold a\par total of HK$1.227 billion (US$158 million) in four separate\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during onshore and offshore trading on Tuesday.\par     The latest move will boost the aggregate balance -- a key\par measure of interbank liquidity -- to a new high of HK$30.513\par billion on Monday.\par     "I noted there was still some U.S. dollar selling against the\par local unit whenever the spot rate edged a little higher," said a\par dealer from a local bank.\par  \par     The Hong Kong dollar        was at 7.7635 at 1700 GMT in New\par York when the HKMA last \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday.\par     It opened on Wednesday at 7.7640 and then firmed to 7.7630/32\par amid U.S.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar selling. By midday it was at 7.7630/31.\par     The HKMA has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at around 7.7630 recently and dealers\par saw that as a support level for the U.S. dollar.\par     Some dealers said strong gains in the Hong Kong stock market\par and a flurry of high profile initial public offerings have\par fuelled an inflow of funds and demand for the local dollar.\par     Traders see a risk of further HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the near\par term as a number of Chinese firms will seek listings in Hong Kong\par next year that will attract more overseas investors.\par     Auditing firm PricewaterhouseCoopers predicted funds raised\par from Hong Kong IPOs could reach HK$100 billion (US$12.8 billion)\par next year.\par     Dealers expect the Hong Kong dollar to hold above its pegged\par against the U.S. dollar in the coming months.\par     "If the stock market continues to rise, the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is\par to remain comparatively strong," said a dealer at a Japanese\par bank.\par     The Hong Kong dollar has strengthened since late September,\par driven by speculation about a revaluation of the Chinese yuan,\par brighter economic prospects, and a weakening of the U.S. dollar.\par     The HKMA has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regularly since then and had\par sold a cumulative HK$30 billion of Hong Kong dollars.\par     As a result, Hong Kong interbank interest rates have fallen\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 below the U.S. dollar rates - the local short-term rates are   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 already near zero - and to a further widening of the discount on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong dollar forwards.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The discount on one-year forwards          widened to 590/570\par pips from Tuesday's close of 575/555 pips.\par     The HKMA is obligated to defend the Hong Kong dollar from\par weakening below its HK$7.80 peg to the U.S. dollar but has no\par mandate to stop it from strengthening above that level.\par                      Morning     