\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar steady after HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2003\par 11:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Dec 30 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar was\par steady on Tuesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA)\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken it, sending the market a strong signal it\par was ready to act to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from getting too strong.\par     The HKMA, the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , sold a\par total of HK$520 million and bought U.S. dollars in two separate\par transactions on Tuesday afternoon in a bid to rein in the local\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength. Real-time data on the HKMA's market\par activity is available on Reuters page .\par     The latest transactions will lift the aggregate balance at\par banks -- a key measure of interbank liquidity -- to a new high\par of HK$28.798 billion on Friday.\par     Dealers said the money market reacted calmly to the HKMA\par actions as the overall market was quiet, with trading desks\par thinly staffed ahead of the year-end.\par     "The market remains thin with little trading momentum.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The\par HKMA action has given strong signals to the market that it is\par committed to exchange rate stability," said a dealer from a\par European bank.\par     He said high demand for Hong Kong dollars might be due to\par the strong stock market and a rush of Chinese IPOs in the\par territory.\par     The benchmark Hang Seng Index        ended up 62.45 points\par to 12,526.74 on Tuesday. Trading volume was heavy at HK$21.9\par billion.\par     However, another dealer from a Japanese bank noted there\par was usually natural demand for local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  towards the end\par of the year.\par  \par     The Hong Kong dollar        traded at 7.7630/31 at 0942\par GMT, compared with 7.7636/38 late on Monday.\par     Meanwhile, the Hong Kong dollar forwards were rangebound.\par     The discount on one-year forwards          were quoted at\par 575/555 late on Tuesday, versus Monday's close at 560/545 pips.\par     Dealers said forwards would remain at a deep discount as\par long as banks' aggregate balance of Hong Kong dollars remained\par so large.\par     Some dealers see the discount on one-year forwards heading\par towards to a new low of 600 pips in the near term.\par     In the cash market, interbank rates remained at low levels.\par     One dealer from a local bank said there was some month-end\par and year-end demand for overnight and tomorrow/next money.\par     The overnight rate was quoted at 0.002-0.005 percent, while\par the tomorrow/next rate at 0.015-0.02 percent.\par     VOLATILITY EXPECTED\par     Looking ahead, dealers said the market was likely to be\par volatile in 2004.\par     "I believe that next year the market will continue to be\par speculative about a yuan revaluation and Hong Kong dollar\par forwards will be affected," said a dealer from a Japanese bank.\par     There was speculations the Hong Kong dollar might move in\par tandem with the yuan should the latter be revalued upward.\par     Hong Kong, a former British colony, has been forging closer\par economic ties with mainland China since it reverted to Chinese\par rule in 1997.\par     U.S. and Chinese officials are expected to meet in Beijing\par in January to discuss U.S. demands that China liberalise its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "There are a lot of things that need to be looking at, such\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 as Hong Kong's annual policy address in early January,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 presidential elections in Taiwan and in the United States, and   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the possibility of a resurgence of SARS," another trader said.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                       At 0900 GMT   At 0330 GMT   At 0945 GMT\par      HK$ SPOT         7.7631/32     7.7634/35     7.7636/38\par      FORWARDS\par      Three-month      -188 / -183   -185 / -183   -186 / -180\par      Six-month        -360 / -350   -360 / -350   -350 / -340\par      One-year         -575 / -555   -570 / -550   -560 / -545\par      INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par      Overnight       0.002 / 0.005 0.005 / 0.005 0.005 / 0.005\par      Three-month      0.09 / 0.10   0.10 / 0.12   0.12 / 0.13\par      Six-month        0.20 / 0.21   0.20 / 0.22   0.21 / 0.23\par      One-year         0.61 / 0.63   0.62 / 0.65   0.63 / 0.68\par      Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Live quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031230dzcu0034a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
