\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA Sells HK$233 Mln In Latest Move To Weaken HK Dlr  \b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2003\par 09:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold HK$520 million in two \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday in its latest effort to cap the strength of the local unit.  \par \par \uc2 As with its earlier \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action had little immediate effect on the market exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was quoted around HK$7.7637 late Tuesday, barely changed from HK$7.7640 Monday.  \par \par \uc2 "There has been little reaction to the HKMA's move, no one really cares, most people are keeping their trading activity down ahead of the (New Year) holiday," a dealer at a local bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Since late September, the Hong Kong dollar has been trading at a rate stronger than its official peg to the U.S. dollar of HK$7.80. This unusual situation has been created by a combination of foreign investment into Hong Kong assets, and speculation about an appreciation in the yuan, using the Hong Kong dollar as a proxy.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system automatically prevents the local unit from weakening away from the peg rate, but there is no such provision in the system to prevent it from strengthening - only the HKMA's discretion to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in individual transactions.  \par \par \uc2 Since September, the HKMA has sold over HK$27 billion, which would buy around US$3.5 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA provides information on its market actions to financial data systems, but doesn't comment on them other than to say it acts as needed to counter market volatility.  \par \par \uc2 -By Raymond Tsoi, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; raymond.tsoi@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Andrew Bullard  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031230dzcu00071\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
