\par\par \b \uc2 HK interbank rates fall on return of IPO funds.  \b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2003\par 10:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     HONG KONG, Dec 19 (Reuters) - Hong Kong interbank rates fell\par across the board on Friday as liquidity improved after more funds\par flowed back from the recent wave of large IPOs in the territory.\par     The overnight rate eased to 0.06-0.12 percent from 0.50-0.56\par percent on Thursday. The one-month rate was quoted at 0.13-0.15\par percent, down from Thursday's 0.20-0.23 percent.\par     "Further downside is expected by early next week after\par another IPO closes," said a trader from a local bank.\par     Front end liquidity has tightened over the past few weeks due\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to massive interest in the IPOs, which have tied up a large  \f28 \par \par \uc2 amount of funds. The offerings included the largest in the world  \par \par \uc2 this year from China Life Insurance Co Ltd .  \par \par \uc2 In the spot market, the Hong Kong dollar weakened  \par \par \uc2 slightly on talk of some investors converting their gains on the  \par \par \uc2 IPOs. "Some investors have been converting their gains after the  \par \par \uc2 recent wave of IPOs, but trade remains very thin," one dealer  \par \par \uc2 said.  \par \par \uc2 The local unit was traded at 7.7660 against the U.S. dollar  \par \par \uc2 at 0900 GMT, versus an intraday high of 7.7665 and 7.7647 late on  \par \par \uc2 Thursday. It remains stubbornly above its 7.8 peg to the U.S.  \par \par \uc2 dollar, despite concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken it.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has strengthened since late September,  \par \par \uc2 driven by market speculation about an appreciation of China's  \par \par \uc2 yuan, an economic recovery and increased fund flows.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong dollar forwards were rangebound in thin trade,  \par \par \uc2 dealers said. The discount on forwards tightened in the early  \par \par \uc2 morning session following a weaker Hong Kong dollar but then  \par \par \uc2 widened on the back of an easing in interbank rates.  \par \par \uc2 "People were selling longer-dated forwards in view of the  \par \par \uc2 ample liquidity and low short-term rates," the European bank  \par \par \uc2 dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 One-year forwards were quoted at -540/-520 pips by late  \par \par \uc2 afternoon versus an earlier -520/-500 pips and little changed  \par \par \uc2 from -530/-515 pips late on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expected forwards to remain at a deep discount given  \par \par \uc2 flush liquidity, with the banks' aggregate balance at over HK$28  \par \par \uc2 billion. The balance has been boosted by a string of injections  \par \par \uc2 from the HKMA.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0849 GMT   At 0323 GMT   At 0830 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7660/62     7.7657/58     7.7645/48\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -182 / -175   -180 / -175   -178 / -173\par     Six-month        -345 / -330   -345 / -330   -350 / -335\par     One-year         -540 / -520   -535 / -515   -530 / -515\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight        0.06 / 0.12   0.32 / 0.37   0.50 / 0.56\par     Three-month      0.15 / 0.17   0.15 / 0.20   0.18 / 0.20\par     Six-month        0.24 / 0.27   0.26 / 0.31   0.27 / 0.30\par     One-year         0.66 / 0.70   0.68 / 0.78   0.68 / 0.73\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on  \f28 \par \par \u