\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr weakens slightly in rangebound trade.   \b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2003\par 05:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Dec 19 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar eased\par slightly against the U.S. unit on Friday morning in quiet trade,\par with some investors converting their gains on a wave of recent\par IPOs in the territory.\par     The local unit        weakened to 7.7665 against the U.S.\par dollar in early trade. It was traded at 7.7657/59 at 0308 GMT,\par versus 7.7647 late on Thursday.\par     "Some investors have been converting their gains after the\par recent wave of IPOs, but trade remains very thin," one dealer\par said.\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has strengthened since late September,\par driven by market speculation about an appreciation of China's\par yuan, an economic recovery and increased fund flows.\par     It remains stubbornly above its 7.8 peg to the U.S. dollar,\par despite concerted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken it.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar forwards were rangebound in thin trade.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The\par discount on forwards opened narrower following a weaker Hong Kong\par dollar but then widened on the back of an easing in front end\par liquidity.\par     One-year forwards were quoted at -535/-515 pips by\par mid-morning versus an earlier -520/-500 pips and little changed\par from -530/-515 pips late on Thursday.\par     Dealers expected forwards to remain at a deep discount given\par flush liquidity, with the banks' aggregate balance at over HK$28\par billion by Friday. The balance has been boosted by a string of\par injections from the HKMA.\par  \par     In the cash market, interbank rates remained soft as funds\par flowed back from recent IPOs.\par     The overnight rate eased to 0.37 percent from Thursday's 0.50\par percent.\par                      Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0323 GMT   At 0830 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7657/58     7.7645/48\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -180 / -175   -178 / -173\par     Six-month        -345 / -330   -350 / -335\par     One-year         -535 / -515   -530 / -515\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight        0.32 / 0.37   0.50 / 0.56\par     Three-month      0.15 / 0.20   0.18 / 0.20\par     Six-month        0.26 / 0.31   0.27 / 0.30\par     One-year         0.68 / 0.78   0.68 / 0.73\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031219dzcj000ki\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
