\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dlr Mkts Late: Hibors Down On Continued High Liquidity  \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2003\par 09:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank offered rates declined again Friday, as more money from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  made its way into the market, and the closing of recent initial public offerings depressed demand for funds.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight Hibor dropped to 0.25%, from 0.65% Thursday, and the one-month Hibor was down to 0.21% from 0.23% previously. Traders said further declines were possible, as the overnight rate had gone below 0.01% before the recent rush of IPOs pushed it up, and there is significant excess liquidity in the system.  \par \par \uc2 The aggregate balance, a measure of interbank liquidity, opened at HK$28.42 billion Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Before the HKMA began its sales of Hong Kong dollars to stem the strengthening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the aggregate balance was typically less than HK$1 billion. It began December at HK$11.6 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar was little changed in the spot and forward markets.  \par \par \uc2 The discount on the benchmark one-year forward contract widened slightly to 540 to 520 below the spot rate, compared to a discount of 530 to 510 previously.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was quoted at HK$7.7655, compared to HK$7.7645 previously. The pair have been trading recently in a range of 7.7600 to 7.7650, and the Hong Kong dollar isn't expected to weaken significantly given continued buying interest in Hong Kong assets.  \par \par \uc2 "Equity-driven inflows are likely to keep the Hong Kong dollar well-supported at the 7.77 level," one trader said.  \par \par \uc2