\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA buys US$64 mln in 1st  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  of the day.  \b0\par\par\uc2 130 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2003\par 16:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     NEW YORK, Dec 17 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Wednesday it had bought around US$64 million\par and sold \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollars, its first \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the day,\par in an attempt to stabilize the local unit's strength.\par  \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  occurred at 10:13 a.m. EST (1513 GMT), the\par HKMA, Hong Kong's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , told Reuters.\par     The HKMA           has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for several days to\par minimize fluctuations in the value of the Hong Kong dollar. On\par Tuesday, it purchased over US$ 1 billion in U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Hong Kong dollar was trading at HK$7.7625/35        to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the U.S. dollar at around 10:42 a.m. EST (1542 GMT).  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031217dzch002n6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
