\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr little moved, front-end rates remain firm.   \b0\par\par\uc2 576 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2003\par 05:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Dec 17 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar was little\par changed on Wednesday morning against the U.S. unit despite\par persistent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par (HKMA) in recent sessions to try to stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par strength.\par     "The spot rate didn't move much after numerous \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par by the HKMA. That implies there is still strong selling pressure\par on U.S. dollars and robust demand for Hong Kong dollars," said a\par dealer from a European bank.\par     The HKMA, the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par and sold HK$7.941 billion in 12 separate moves during onshore and\par offshore trading hours over Tuesday afternoon to early Wednesday.\par  \par     Since Friday, it has sold a total of HK$15.464 billion and\par bought U.S. dollars to rein in the robust local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will lift the aggregate balance -- a key\par measure of interbank liquidity -- to new highs of HK$27.805\par billion by Thursday.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers have attributed recent strong demand for the local\par unit to an overwhelming investor response to a string of initial\par public offerings (IPOs) in the territory.\par     "There is market talk that there will be some new share\par issues next year, I think some 'hot money' is parking in Hong\par Kong," one trader said.\par     Chinese firms likely to list in Hong Kong next year include\par Minsheng Bank, Ping An Insurance, Semiconductor Manufacturing\par Corp International and Air China.\par     The Hong Kong dollar        was traded at 7.7637/40 at 0300\par GMT, versus 7.7630 late on Tuesday.\par     In the cash market, interbank rates were mixed. Front-end\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 liquidity remained tight as some funds were still tied up by   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 recent IPOs. Longer-dated rates eased given a large aggregate   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 balance and following softer U.S. bond yields, dealers said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The overnight and tomorrow/next interbank rates were quoted   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 at one percent. Meanwhile, the one-year rate eased to 0.68-0.75   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent from Tuesday's 0.73-0.78 percent.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Some receiving banks for the IPOs are still holding up the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 liquidity, rates are expected to ease by early next week," the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European bank dealer said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong dollar forwards were rangebound at large discounts.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The overnight and tomorrow/next forwards were trading at around   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 par to a slight premium, tracking short-term interbank rates.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "A good part of this strength is due to inflows related to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IPOs. The new event that has led to fresh lows in the one-year   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 forwards especially, has been IPO-related," said James Malcolm,   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase in Singapore.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The discount on longer-dated forwards narrowed following   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 sporadic U.S. dollar-buying in the spot market by the mid-morning   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 session, dealers said.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     One-year forwards          were trading at -500/-480 pips,\par narrowing from -540/-520 pips late on Tuesday.\par                     Morning       Previous Close\par                     At 0345 GMT   At 0904 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT        7.7640/50     7.7629/30\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month     -180 / -170   -180 / -173\par     Six-month       -345 / -330   -345 / -335\par     One-year        -500 / -480   -540 / -520\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight       0.87 / 1.00   0.43 / 0.50\par     Three-month     0.18 / 0.21   0.19 / 0.22\par     Six-month       0.25 / 0.31   0.31 / 0.33\par     One-year        0.68 / 0.75   0.73 / 0.78\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031217dzch000my\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
