\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Asia:Investors Snap Up Blns of HK Dlrs Sold By HKMA  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Raymond Tsoi  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 898 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2003\par 10:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Despite the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  increasing the size and frequency of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar has shown few signs of giving up its recent strength as the market easily absorbs a flood of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the HKMA.  \par \par \uc2 It seems the HKMA's strategy of upping the dosage of its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but merely prevent it from strengthening further in a market dominated by persistent fund inflows attracted by investment opportunities in Hong Kong.  \par \par \uc2 "Foreign investors must have spotted some opportunities to invest or speculate in Hong Kong's financial markets or other types of assets," Hang Seng Bank senior economist Henry Tsoi said.  \par \par \uc2 "They could be positioning such trades currently, and looking to cash out over ... a few months to a year," Tsoi said, adding that a quick reversal of these inflows is unlikely as a result.  \par \par \uc2 Since the local unit strayed from its U.S. dollar peg rate of HK$7.80 in late September amid talk of yuan revaluation, the HKMA has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  from time to time to contain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.  \par \par \uc2 From a usual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  size of about US$100 million-US$200 million per day, the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has upped the size of its U.S. dollar purchases to about US$500 million to US$1 billion a day in recent sessions, usually in multiple transactions.  \par \par \uc2 "Through these larger and more frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the HKMA probably wanted to show the market it is very committed to maintaining \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 As committed as the HKMA may be to the city's 20-year-old linked exchange system, foreign investors have their own objectives and trading plans.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Investors Buying HK Dlrs To Position For Investments \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indeed, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar hardly budged after all these \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent weeks, sticking most of the time to a narrow range between HK$7.7600 and HK$7.7650.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  did little to boost the U.S. dollar, this probably implied there are strong fund inflows offsetting those transactions," the trader said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "These fund inflows could be part of efforts by foreign investors to build up their Hong Kong dollar positions for future investment in local equities and initial public offerings next year," he added.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HKMA Chief Executive Joseph Yam attributed the recent influx of foreign funds partly to a flurry of IPO activity.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Among recent IPOs, Great Wall Automobile Holding Co. (2333.HK) and China Life Insurance Co. (2628.HK) were two large initial share sales that attracted heavy oversubscription, tying up billions of Hong Kong dollars.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said the HKMA may have noticed significant IPO-driven fund inflows and has been acting more aggressively in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to neutralize them.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It may also be part of the HKMA's strategy to depress Hong Kong dollar interest rates through larger injections, thus reducing the local unit's attractiveness to foreigners.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One-month Hong Kong interbank offered rates were quoted near zero, at 0.28% Wednesday afternoon.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, traders doubt if lower interest rates will make much difference, as potential gains from Hong Kong dollar assets should easily make up for reduced interest return in the current bull market for shares and amid rising property prices.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Traders Raise Possibility Of Negative Rates \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The benchmark Hang Seng index has gained more than 40% since its near-five-year low in the spring as the city emerges from a short recession in the third quarter.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Continued economic improvement led by tourism gains, export expansion and growth in domestic consumption is likely to preserve the attraction of Hong Kong shares for foreign investors in the coming months, analysts said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 To a lesser extent, inflows may be attracted by the city's zero-tariff access to the China market granted under Hong Kong's trade pact with Beijing.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The economic sentiment has improved substantially after a series of favorable mainland polices toward Hong Kong, including the relaxed restrictions on individual travel and the Closer Economic Partnership Arrangement," Daniel Chan of DBS Bank (HK) said. Foreign investors may expect these moves to increase their opportunities to make profits in the territory.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, the HKMA's recent actions imply it won't tolerate an appreciation in the local unit beyond HK$7.76 against the U.S. dollar, a resistance level for the local unit most traders expect will stay intact.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The HKMA seems to be very dedicated to this level," the trader said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It can even introduce negative interest rates to penalize banks keeping too much of a Hong Kong dollar surplus, forcing them to convert their Hong Kong dollars into U.S. dollars."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Although Yam said he wouldn't rule out introducing such deposit charges on banks' surplus balance in their clearing accounts with the HKMA, he doesn't yet envisage the need to do so, and he still hopes that the market will adjust itself.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Raymond Tsoi, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; raymond.tsoi@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Raymond Tsoi has been a reporter at Dow Jones Newswires for more than a year. Prior to that he spent more than 10-years selling fixed-income securities.)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by John Viljoen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 4258 5095  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031217dzch000dj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
