\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dlr Mkts Late: Forward Discounts Narrow On SARS Fears  \b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2003\par 09:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong dollar forwards discounts narrowed slightly Wednesday on concerns about the return of SARS to the region.  \par \par \uc2 Health officials in Taiwan said Wednesday a 44-year-old male medical researcher tested positive for severe acute respiratory syndrome and has been isolated at a local hospital.  \par \par \uc2 Although officials downplayed the likelihood of another outbreak of the deadly disease, stressing that this appeared to be an isolated case, local traders remained concerned SARS may return to haunt the region, including Hong Kong.  \par \par \uc2 The one-year contract was quoted at 500-480 below the spot rate, compared with 510 to 500 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Further aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently has also put upward pressure on forwards.  \par \par \uc2 The quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold HK$7.94 billion Tuesday, the largest amount it has sold on a single day since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strayed from the U.S. dollar peg rate in late September.  \par \par \uc2 SARS fears and HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  combined to push the local unit lower, although only by a small margin.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was quoted at HK$7.7638, compared with HK$7.7627 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders, however, expect foreign inflows to persist in the near term, as investors buy shares on the Hong Kong stock market and participate in a series of initial public offerings.  \par \par \uc2 "Such potential inflows may keep the U.S. dollar firmly capped around HK$7.77 over coming months," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong interbank offered rates moved higher despite the HKMA's injections, as traders preferred to have surplus funds on hand amid the uncertainty over SARS.  \par \par \uc2 "Banks are borrowing most actively in short-dated funds up to one month," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The one-month Hibor was quoted at 0.28%, compared with 0.25% Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Long-term interbank funds were relatively steady, with the 12-month Hibor quoted at 0.79%, compared with 0.80% previously.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong Exchange Fund note yields were little moved.  \par \par \uc2 The 10-year EF note was quoted at 4.38%, compared with 4.39% Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                   Latest        Late Tuesday \par Overnight Hibor   1.00%           0.80% \par 1-mo Hibor        0.28%           0.25% \par 3-mo Hibor        0.28%           0.23% \par 1-yr Hibor        0.79%           0.80% \par USD/HKD Spot      HK$7.7638       HK$7.7627 \par 6-mo HKD Fwd      -345 to -335   -340 to -325 \par 1-yr HKD Fwd      -500 to -480   -510 to -500 \par  \par 4.32% EF Note Due Dec. 2, 2013: \par  \par    Price: 99.93 Vs 99.88 \par    Yield: 4.38% Vs 4.39% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Raymond Tsoi, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; raymond.tsoi@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by John Viljoen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1053 4178  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031217dzch000ap\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
