\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA Sells HK$2.14 Bln More In Latest  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 181 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2003\par 09:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold an additional HK$2.14 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Tuesday afternoon, buying about US$275 million, in its latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar against its U.S. counterpart.  \par \par \uc2 Combined with earlier sales Monday, the HKMA's latest move brings its total sales for the day to HK$3.26 billion, which would buy about US$420 million.  \par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's spot exchange rate remained largely unaffected by the HKMA's increasing activity. The U.S. dollar was quoted around HK$7.7627 Tuesday afternoon, roughly the level it was at earlier Tuesday and Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system automatically prevents the local unit from weakening away from the peg rate, but there is no such provision in the system to prevent it from strengthening - only the HKMA's discretion to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in individual transactions.  \par \par \uc2 -By Andrew Batson, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; andrew.batson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Andrew Bullard  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031216dzcg000bf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
