\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr steady, ignores HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 446 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2003\par 04:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Dec 16 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar was little\par changed and remained above its peg with the U.S. unit on Tuesday\par morning despite a concerted round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong\par Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) to weaken it, underpinned by\par bullish sentiment in Hong Kong's stock market.\par     The HKMA, the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par 13 times during onshore and offshore trading over Monday\par afternoon to early Tuesday morning. It sold a total of HK$4.565\par billion and bought U.S. dollars in a bid to stabilise the local\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength.\par     Since Friday, the HKMA has sold nearly HK$7.523 billion. The\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will lift the aggregate balance -- a key measure of\par interbank liquidity -- to rise to HK$19.863 billion on Wednesday.\par  \par     "I think the recent influx of funds are for stock\par investment," one trader at a local bank said.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said demand for the local unit was likely to remain\par strong following very successful, large share issues in Hong Kong\par by fast-growing mainland Chinese companies.\par     The Hong Kong dollar traded at 7.7629/30 against the U.S.\par unit at 0313 GMT, unchanged from 7.7630 late on Monday.\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has strengthened since late September,\par driven by speculation about the revaluation of the renminbi,\par brighter domestic economic prospects and increased fund flows.\par     Bearish sentiment towards the U.S. dollar on persistent\par concerns over a ballooning U.S. current account deficit, have\par also lent support to the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards deepened on the\par back of surging liquidity in the aggregate balance.\par     One-year forwards were quoted at -480/-470 pips, widening\par from -450/-430 pips.\par     In the cash market, players were still focusing on front end\par liquidity as some funds were still locked up by the receiving\par banks for a spate of recent initial public offerings.\par     The overnight rate softened to 0.25-0.37 percent from an\par earlier 0.62-0.87 percent after some banks released liquidity.\par                 Morning       Previous Close\par                     At 0330 GMT   At 0900 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT        7.7629/30     7.7629/30\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month     -175 / -170   -175 / -170\par     Six-month       -330 / -315   -315 / -305\par     One-year        -480 / -460   -450 / -430\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight       0.25 / 0.40   0.75 / 0.87\par     Three-month     0.17 / 0.22   0.18 / 0.23\par     Six-month       0.31 / 0.37   0.33 / 0.38\par     One-year        0.75 / 0.81   0.82 / 0.87\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters contributor page .\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031216dzcg000xd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
