\par\par \b \uc2 WRAP: HKMA Sells HK$1.5 Bln In 2nd Day Of  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrew Batson and Raymond Tsoi  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 527 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2003\par 10:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold Hong Kong dollars and bought U.S. dollars again Monday, in a renewed bout of market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  intended to keep the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening against its U.S. counterpart.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA, which acts as the city's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and implementer of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, sold a total of HK$1.5 billion Monday afternoon in a series of transactions, buying about US$190 million. The latest round of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  follows several sales Friday that totaled HK$2.96 billion, which bought around US$380 million.  \par \par \uc2 Yet Monday's sales, like the previous ones, appeared to have little immediate effect on the Hong Kong dollar's exchange rate. The U.S. dollar was quoted around HK$7.7630 for most of Friday and Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA has previously acted to prevent the U.S. dollar from falling below HK$7.76, but that didn't seem to be a major issue recently with the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets quiet.  \par \par \uc2 "It's very difficult for us to understand their thinking," a Hong Kong-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said. "There hasn't been much fluctuation in the rate recently."  \par \par \uc2 "The lack of movement in the spot market may imply there are fund inflows offsetting the HKMA's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," another trader with a local bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Since late September, the Hong Kong dollar has been trading at a rate stronger than its official peg to the U.S. dollar of HK$7.80, an unusual situation driven by a combination of flows of foreign investment into Hong Kong assets, and speculation on the possible appreciation of the yuan, using the Hong Kong dollar as a proxy.  \par \par \uc2 Most market participants don't anticipate a return to the peg rate until the fund inflows to Hong Kong, which have been supporting the stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reverse.  \par \par \uc2 There is no immediate sign that will happen, especially given the recent wave of highly popular initial public offerings from China-related companies such as China Life Insurance Co.  \par \par \uc2 So rather than actively work to return the Hong Kong dollar to its peg rate, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  occasionally in the market to keep the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening too far away from the peg.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system automatically prevents the local unit from weakening away from the peg rate, but there is no such provision in the system to prevent it from strengthening - only the HKMA's discretion to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in individual transactions.  \par \par \uc2 Friday's and Monday's sales bring the HKMA's total sales since the September strengthening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to HK$15.48 billion, which would buy just under US$2 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA provides information on its market actions to financial data systems, but doesn't comment on them other than to say it acts as needed to counter market volatility.  \par \par \uc2 -By Andrew Batson and Raymond Tsoi, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; andrew.batson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Andrew Bullard  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031215dzcf000er\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
