\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dlr Mkts Late: HK Dlr Flat After HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2003\par 09:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was little changed Monday, despite fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the city's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was quoted at HK$7.7630, roughly the same level at which the HKMA is believed to have sold Hong Kong dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a total of HK$2.96 billion in multiple transactions Friday, followed by another sale of HK$1.32 billion Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the lack of an automatic mechanism to cap the upside of the Hong Kong dollar under the city's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, the HKMA has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a discretionary basis to prevent the U.S. dollar from falling below HK$7.76 in recent weeks, although that didn't seem to be the trigger for the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets being quiet.  \par \par \uc2 "It's very difficult for us to understand the HKMA's thinking," a Hong Kong-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said. "There hasn't been much fluctuation in the rate recently."  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect a narrow trading band of HK$7.7600-HK$7.7700 this week.  \par \par \uc2 Interbank liquidity is expected to increase after the HKMA injections. The aggregate balance, the key measure of interbank excess funds, will likely reach over HK$15 billion when those trades are settled Tuesday, putting downward pressure on Hong Kong interbank offered rates.  \par \par \uc2 The closing of several major initial public offerings also relieved the demand for funds in the market, contributing to the fall in Hibors.  \par \par \uc2 The one-month Hibor was quoted at 0.28%, down from 0.34% Friday. The 12-month Hibor was quoted at 0.88%, compared with 0.91% previously.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong dollar forwards were little changed, with the one-year contract being quoted at 440-430 below spot, compared with 445-435 Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Long-dated Hong Kong Exchange Fund note yields edged higher, following U.S. Treasury yields. The 10-year bond was quoted at 4.45%, compared with 4.39% Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Short maturity bonds were relatively well bid given the drop in Hibors. The two-year bond was quoted at 1.32%, unchanged from Friday.  \par \par \uc2 1053 4178  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031215dzcf000cd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
