\par\par \b \uc2 WRAP: HKMA Sold HK$2.96B Fri In  \highlight22\uc2 Currency Interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrew Batson  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 448 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2003\par 04:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a total of HK$2.96 billion, buying around US$380 million, in eight transactions Friday intended to weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong business day saw sales of HK$932 million, with the remainder coming during London and New York trading hours. None of the sales had a marked effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's spot exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 Early Monday, the U.S. dollar was quoted around HK$7.7630, roughly the same level at which the HKMA is believed to have sold Hong Kong dollars. The HKMA has previously acted to prevent the U.S. dollar from falling below HK$7.76, but that didn't seem to be an issue last week with the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets quiet.  \par \par \uc2 "It's very difficult for us to understand their thinking," a Hong Kong-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said. "There hasn't been much fluctuation in the rate recently."  \par \par \uc2 Since late September, the Hong Kong dollar has been trading at a rate stronger than its official peg to the U.S. dollar at HK$7.80, an unusual situation driven by a combination of flows of foreign investment into Hong Kong assets, and speculation on the possible appreciation of the yuan, using the Hong Kong dollar as a proxy.  \par \par \uc2 Most market participants don't anticipate a return to the peg rate until the fund inflows to Hong Kong, which have been supporting the stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reverse.  \par \par \uc2 There is no immediate sign that will happen, especially given the recent wave of highly popular initial public offerings from China-related companies such as China Life Insurance Co. Friday, the Chinese insurer said it would price the shares in the world's biggest initial public offering this year at near the top end of the range.  \par \par \uc2 Rather than actively work to return the Hong Kong dollar to its peg rate, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  occasionally in the market to keep the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening too far away from the peg.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system automatically prevents the local unit from weakening away from the peg rate, but there is no such system to prevent it from strengthening - only the HKMA's discretion to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA provides information on its market actions to financial data systems, but doesn't comment on them other than to say it acts as needed to counter market volatility.  \par \par \uc2 -By Andrew Batson, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; andrew.batson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by John Viljoen  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031215dzcf0003j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
