\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr steady despite numerous HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 616 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2003\par 11:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Dec 15 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar was\par steady and moved in a very tight range on Monday, shrugging off\par numerous \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par (HKMA) to weaken it as money for stock investments flows in.\par     The HKMA, the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to sell a total of HK$1.5 billion and bought U.S. dollars in\par three separate moves on Monday afternoon in a bid to stabilise\par the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength. The moves followed nine\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during onshore and offshore trading over Friday\par to early Monday morning.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will lift the aggregate balance -- a key\par measure of interbank liquidity -- to a historic high of\par HK$16.79 billion on Wednesday.\par     Dealers said demand for the local unit was likely to stay\par strong following very successful, large share issues in Hong\par Kong by fast-growing mainland Chinese companies.\par  \par     "The stock market is very bullish and funds are flowing\par in," said a dealer from a European bank.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Recent initial public offerings included the world's\par largest this year, from China Life Insurance , which\par raised $3 billion.\par     Gold miner Fujian Zijin Mining Industry Co Ltd\par kicked off a share sale to retail investors last Thursday to\par raise up to HK$1.15 billion.\par     The Hong Kong dollar        shuffled between 7.7629-7.7633\par on Monday. It was traded at 7.7630 at 0956 GMT, unchanged from\par Friday in Asian trading.\par     "I see the Hong Kong dollar remaining strong on hopes for\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more fund inflows. If China's economy continues to be strong\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that will benefit Hong Kong. The U.S. economy has shown signs\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of improvement, and people expect Hong Kong's economy to\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The United States is the territory's second largest trading\par partner after mainland China.\par     Hong Kong's economy has shown signs of picking up in recent\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par months with the signing of a closer economic cooperation pact\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with mainland China, the lifting of restrictions on individual\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par mainland visitors coming to Hong Kong and the recent move to\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par allow Hong Kong banks to conduct yuan-denominated business.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interbank market, front end liquidity tightened\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slightly as some IPOs funds were still being locked up by the\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The overnight and tomorrow/next interbank rates were quoted\par at 0.75-0.87 percent and 0.70-0.90 percent respectively.\par     "Rates will ease after the IPOs are over. The USD spot rate\par may edged higher if investors convert their funds," one dealer\par from a Japanese bank said.\par     But he expected the spot rate to move between 7.76-7.77 in\par the near term.\par     Hong Kong dollar forwards were range-bound in thin trade\par and were tracking the movement in short-term rates.\par     The discount on one-year forwards          traded at\par 450/430 pips by late afternoon, versus 460 pips in early trade,\par and flat from Friday's close.\par                     Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                     At 0900 GMT   At 0245 GMT   At 0854 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT        7.7629/30     7.7629/30     7.7630/35\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month     -175 / -170   -180 / -175   -182 / -172\par     Six-month       -315 / -305   -325 / -315   -320 / -310\par     One-year        -450 / -430   -460 / -440   -450 / -430\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight       0.75 / 0.87   0.25 / 0.37   0.50 / 0.50\par     Three-month     0.18 / 0.23   0.17 / 0.20   0.15 / 0.20\par     Six-month       0.33 / 0.38   0.31 / 0.34   0.30 / 0.35\par     One-year        0.82 / 0.87   0.78 / 0.82   0.70 / 0.81\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Live quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Reuters contributor page .\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031215dzcf00212\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
