\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr remains strong despite Saddam's capture.   \b0\par\par\uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2003\par 04:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Dec 15 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar remained\par stubbornly above its pegged exchange rate on Monday morning\par despite a firmer U.S. dollar against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  following\par the capture of former Iraqi leader Saddam Hussein, and numerous\par attempts by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the local unit.\par     Dealers said demand for the local unit was likely to stay\par strong following very successful, large share issues in Hong Kong\par by fast-growing mainland Chinese companies.\par     "The U.S. unit and U.S. bond yields rose slightly on Saddam's\par news, but Hong Kong money rates didn't follow the move," said a\par dealer at a European bank.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the territory's de facto\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in nine separate moves during onshore\par and offshore trading over Friday to early Monday. It bought a\par total of US$381 million and sold HK$2.958 billion in a bid to\par stabilise the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     As a result, the aggregate balance -- a key measure of\par interbank liquidity -- will rise to a historic high of HK$15.3\par billion on Tuesday.\par     Dealers said the strong capital inflows could be attributed\par to the overwhelming response to recent initial public offerings\par of stock, including the world's largest this year from China Life\par Insurance , which raised US$3 billion.\par     "Market attention is still focusing on the influx of funds. I\par expect the strength of the local unit to persist on the back of\par the stock rally," another dealer said.\par     "Recent new share issues have been greatly oversubscribed,\par and that will attract more foreign funds to Hong Kong," the\par dealer added.\par  \par     The Hong Kong dollar        traded at 7.7631 against the U.S.\par unit at 0230 GMT, versus 7.7630 late on Friday in Asian trading.\par     The Hong Kong dollar has strengthened since late September,\par driven by speculation about the revaluation of the renminbi,\par brighter economic prospects and increased fund flows.\par     The HKMA has said it will not formally set a limit on how\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strong it will allow the Hong Kong dollar to get, but it is   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 committed to preventing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from weakening below the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HK$7.80 per U.S. unit mark.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The discount on one-year forwards          widened to 460/440\par pips from Friday's close of 450/430 pips.\par                     Morning       Previous Close\par                     At 0245 GMT   At 0854 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT        7.7629/30     7.7630/35\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month     -180 / -175   -182 / -172\par     Six-month       -325 / -315   -320 / -310\par     One-year        -460 / -440   -450 / -430\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight       0.25 / 0.37   0.50 / 0.50\par     Three-month     0.17 / 0.20   0.15 / 0.20\par     Six-month       0.31 / 0.34   0.30 / 0.35\par     One-year        0.78 / 0.82   0.70 / 0.81\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA