\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA Sells HK$776 Mln In Latest Move To Weaken  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2003\par 08:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday sold HK$776 million, buying about US$100 million, in a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transaction intended to weaken the local unit against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  happened when the U.S. dollar was trading around HK$7.7630. A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't have a major impact on the market, with little change in the spot rate after the sale.  \par \par \uc2 It wasn't immediately clear why the HKMA chose to make the sale at that level. In the past it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the HK$7.76 level.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's spot exchange rate has been stronger than its peg rate of HK$7.80 to the U.S. dollar since late September, an unusual situation driven by a combination of strong foreign investor interest in Hong Kong's stock and property markets, and speculation on the possible appreciation of the Chinese yuan, using the Hong Kong dollar as a proxy.  \par \par \uc2 Most market participants don't anticipate a return to the peg rate until the strong fund inflows to Hong Kong, which have been supporting the stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reverse. And there is no immediate sign that will happen, especially given the recent wave of highly popular initial public offerings from China-related companies.  \par \par \uc2 Rather than actively work to return the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar to its peg rate, the HKMA has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  occasionally in the market to keep it from strengthening too far away from the peg.  \par \par \uc2 -By Andrew Batson and Raymond Tsoi, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; andrew.batson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by John Viljoen  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031212dzcc0006t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
