\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar off morning lows, eye US jobs data.   \b0\par\par\uc2 468 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2003\par 10:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Dec 5 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar drifted\par slightly lower on Friday but edged off early lows as\par followthrough buying for the greenback petered out and market\par players awaited U.S. employment data later in the day.\par     "The market has been range trading and activity was thin.\par People stayed on the sidelines ahead of the U.S. jobs data," said\par a dealer from a European bank.\par     The report at 1330 GMT is expected to show 150,000 new\par non-farm jobs were created in November and an unchanged\par unemployment rate of 6.0 percent.\par     "Expectations for good numbers have been rising, fuelled by\par recent robust economic figures. A strong reading on U.S. payrolls\par will stoke speculation of a Fed rate hike," the dealer said.\par  \par     Dealers expect lacklustre trade into the year-end as many\par market makers close their books and take off for the holidays.\par     "Investors are likely to avoid taking aggressive positions\par into the thin year-end market.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  I expect the USD/HKD spot rate to\par remain in a 7.76-7.77 range," another trader said.\par     At 0830 GMT, the local unit        traded around 7.7652/54\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per U.S. dollar, versus 7.7668 at 0306 GMT in morning trade and\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par little changed from 7.7654 at 0848 GMT on Thursday. It was still\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par notably stronger than the HK$7.80 linked exfhange rate.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After a sharp strengthening in late September, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar has slowly retreated, aided by a spate of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, dealers said the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  faces a key\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resistance barrier at 7.77. The spot rate has made several\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attempts to break above that level in recent months but has\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Hong Kong dollar forwards were rangebound in a tight band on\par Friday.\par     The discount on one-year forwards          ended at 420/400\par pips by late afternoon, compared with 400/380 pips in early\par morning session and flat from Thursday's close.\par                     Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                     At 0830 GMT   At 0316 GMT   At 0830 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT        7.7652/54     7.7666/68     7.7655/59\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month     -178 / -173   -178 / -175   -180 / -175\par     Six-month       -300 / -290   -300 / -290   -305 / -295\par     One-year        -420 / -400   -410 / -390   -420 / -400\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight      0.001 / 0.001 0.004 / 0.005 0.003 / 0.005\par     Three-month     0.17 / 0.21   0.17 / 0.18   0.17 / 0.22\par     Six-month       0.40 / 0.45   0.40 / 0.42   0.39 / 0.46\par     One-year        0.97 / 1.05   0.97 / 1.05   1.04 / 1.09\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters contributor page .\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031205dzc5002hb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
