\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong dollar inches lower in light trade.   \b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2003\par 04:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Dec 5 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar edged\par slightly lower on Friday morning amid some sporadic buying of the\par U.S. unit ahead of the year end, but dealers said volumes\par remained thin.\par     "There has been sporadic corporate USD buying in recent\par sessions. But I think the market will range trade amid a lack of\par fresh market moving news," said a dealer from a local bank.\par     The Hong Kong unit        weakened to 7.7668 per U.S. dollar\par at 0306 GMT, versus 7.7654 at 0848 GMT on Thursday, but was still\par stronger than the 7.80 linked exchange rate.\par  \par     Hong Kong dollar forwards discounts tightened slightly\par following the weakening in the local unit.\par     The discount on one-year forwards          narrowed to\par 410/390 pips from 420/400 pips late on Thursday.\par     "Investors are likely to avoid taking aggressive positions\par into the thin year-end market. I expect the USD/HKD spot rate to\par remain in a 7.76-7.77 range," another trader said.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  faces a key resistance\par barrier at 7.77. The spot rate has made several attempts to break\par above that level in recent months but has failed each time.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the de-facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  repeatedly in the market since late September to\par try to stabilise the strengthening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The HKMA has said it will not formally set a limit on how\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strong it will allow the Hong Kong dollar to get, but it is   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 committed to preventing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from weakening below the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HK$7.80 per dollar mark.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The market is looking ahead to the U.S. November employment\par report due at 1330 GMT for fresh clues.\par                     Morning       Previous Close\par                     At 0316 GMT   At 0830 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT        7.7666/68     7.7655/59\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month     -178 / -175   -180 / -175\par     Six-month       -300 / -290   -305 / -295\par     One-year        -410 / -390   -420 / -400\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight      0.004 / 0.005 0.003 / 0.005\par     Three-month     0.17 / 0.18   0.17 / 0.22\par     Six-month       0.40 / 0.42   0.39 / 0.46\par     One-year        0.97 / 1.05   1.04 / 1.09\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031205dzc500167\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
