\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA Advisory Group: No Need To Change HK  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Board  \b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2003\par 03:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The recent strengthening of the Hong Kong dollar away from its peg to the U.S. dollar doesn't create a need for any changes to the city's 20-year-old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, advisers to Hong Kong's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.  \par \par \uc2 The Exchange Fund Advisory Committee's subcommittee on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a meeting last month that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent use of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to "dampen excessive market volatility" in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were "appropriate." Systemic changes aren't necessary, it said.  \par \par \uc2 Under Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, the HKMA is obliged to buy the Hong Kong dollar from banks at the peg rate of HK$7.80 to the U.S. dollar, an automatic mechanism that prevents the Hong Kong dollar from weakening against the U.S. dollar. However the HKMA has no obligation to sell the Hong Kong dollar at that rate, so the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  can become stronger than the peg.  \par \par \uc2 Since the Hong Kong dollar first strengthened away from the peg rate on Sept. 22, the HKMA has bought more than US$1 billion in a series of market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , usually timed to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar from strengthening beyond HK$7.76 to the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Now that the Hong Kong dollar has spent an extended period trading away from the peg, some economists and market participants have criticized the one-sided \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board for introducing uncertainty into the territory's exchange rate regime.  \par \par \uc2 Current and former HKMA officials have said, however, they prefer to maintain the flexibility on defending the strong side of the peg that the current system gives them.  \par \par \uc2 The advisory committee found no ill effects from the stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Members observed that the impact of the strengthening of the dollar on the real economy had been minimal," the report of the committee's meeting said. "It appeared that the concerns in the market about deflation, the budget deficit and unemployment had for the time being subsided."  \par \par \uc2 The committee's meeting was held Nov. 7, but the record of its discussions wasn't released by the HKMA until late Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Andrew Batson, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; andrew.batson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Andrew Bullard  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031205dzc50002h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
