\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr weakens slightly in choppy trade.   \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2003\par 05:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Dec 4 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar weakened\par slightly amid some interest in the U.S. unit on Thursday morning\par but dealers expected the market to remain rangebound in the near\par term.\par     "Trades are expected to be thin as the year end approaches.\par Thin activity has exaggerated moves," said a dealer from a\par European bank.\par     The Hong Kong unit          weakened to 7.7660 to the dollar\par before settling at 7.7651/53 by 0340 GMT in choppy trade. That\par compared with 7.7631 at 0927 GMT on Wednesday.\par  \par     The discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards          narrowed\par to 420/400 pips from 460/440 pips late on Wednesday.\par     "I think the market is in rangebound trade. People are buying\par at lows and selling at highs," another trader said.\par     He expected the Hong Kong dollar to remain moving between\par 7.76 and 7.77, with one-year forwards trapped in a -450 to -350\par pips range.\par     Some dealers said the Hong Kong dollar could climb again as\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 funds continue to flow in for upcoming initial public offerings   \par \par \uc2 in the territory and as investors remain bearish on the U.S.   \par \par \uc2 dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Renewed strength for the HK dollar on Wednesday coincided   \par \par \uc2 with a sharp drop for the U.S. unit against all major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 However, dealers said the upside for the local unit would be   \par \par \uc2 limited amid fears of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been trying to drag the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 back to its 7.80 peg to the greenback.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Morning       Previous Close\par                     At 0315 GMT   At 0900 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT        7.7653/58     7.7624/34\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month     -180 / -175   -182 / -180\par     Six-month       -300 / -290   -315 / -305\par     One-year        -420 / -400   -460 / -440\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight      0.005 / 0.006 0.005 / 0.006\par     Three-month     0.17 / 0.22   0.17 / 0.19\par     Six-month       0.39 / 0.46   0.38 / 0.41\par     One-year        0.95 / 1.06   0.95 / 1.00\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031204dzc4000um\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
