\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dlr Mkts Late: EF Note Yields Rise Before US Jobs Data  \b0\par\par\uc2 458 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2003\par 09:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong Exchange Fund note yields rose modestly Thursday on position adjustment ahead of the U.S.'s November employment data due Friday, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The yield on the two-year EF note was quoted at 1.61%, up from 1.59% Wednesday. The 10-year EF note yield was quoted at 4.60%, up from 4.58% previously.  \par \par \uc2 "Given the recent strength in the Institute for Supply Management employment index, the U.S. jobs data may confirm labor market conditions are getting better, raising the chance of a tightening in interest rate policy next year," a trader said.  \par \par \uc2 That prompted position adjustment, pushing bond yields higher.  \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar weakened a tad after meeting tough resistance near the HK$7.76 level.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar late Thursday was quoted at HK$7.7644, compared with HK$7.7620 late Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "Some players closed their short U.S. dollar positions after having failed to push it below HK$7.760, and amid concerns the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to boost the U.S. dollar," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Still, few expect the U.S. dollar to strengthen beyond HK$7.77 given its recent slide against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as well as continuing equity-driven fund inflows into the local stock market.  \par \par \uc2 The discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards narrowed following the slight weakening in the Hong Kong dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The one-year contract was quoted at 425-400 below the spot, compared with 460-440 Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 A sharp narrowing of the discount is considered unlikely, however, as excess liquidity in the interbank market will keep interest rates on the Hong Kong dollar well below those on the U.S. dollar, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Long-dated Hong Kong interbank offered rates rose slightly as the local unit weakened. The 12-month Hibor was quoted at 1.08%, up from 1.02% Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Short-maturity Hibors, by contrast, stayed near historical lows under the weight of excess funds. The one-month Hibor was quoted at 0.10%, compared with 0.09% Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                   Latest        Late Wednesday \par Overnight Hibor   0.01%            0.02% \par 1-mo Hibor        0.10%            0.09% \par 3-mo Hibor        0.24%            0.19% \par 1-yr Hibor        1.08%            1.02% \par USD/HKD Spot      HK$7.7644        HK$7.7620 \par 6-mo HKD Fwd      -311 to -301     -320 to -313 \par 1-yr HKD Fwd      -425 to -400     -460 to -440 \par  \par 4.32% EF Note Due Dec. 2, 2013: \par  \par    Price: 98.23 Vs 98.34 \par    Yield: 4.60% Vs 4.58% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Raymond Tsoi, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; raymond.tsoi@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Andrew Bullard  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1053 4178  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031204dzc40009u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
