\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr remains firm despite HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2003\par 04:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Dec 3 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar remained\par firm on Wednesday morning despite fresh attempts by the Hong Kong\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken it and bring it back toward its\par pegged exchange rate.\par     "As long as the U.S. dollar remains weak against major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , I don't think we're going to see the (upward)\par pressure on the Hong Kong dollar come off," said a senior trader\par at a Japanese bank in Hong Kong.\par     The euro hit record highs against the dollar for the fourth\par straight trading day on Wednesday as concerns about the U.S.\par current account deficit and Washington's handling of post-war\par Iraq overshadowed strong U.S. economic data.\par  \par     "Allowing the Hong Kong dollar to remain strong is not good\par for the economy and is not good for the peg," he said.\par     The HKMA, the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 to buy about US$94 million and sell \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollars in two   \f28 \par \par \uc2 separate moves in offshore trading over Tuesday and early   \par \par \uc2 Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 "The HKMA is trying to draw a line in the sand and tell the   \par \par \uc2 market that it is gradually moving the point at which it will   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher," said a dealer at a large European bank in Hong   \par \par \uc2 Kong.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The 20-year-old \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg is widely seen as the bedrock of\par Hong Kong's financial stability.\par     The local unit had firmed to around HK$7.7590 per U.S. dollar\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in overnight trade according to Reuters charts. By mid-morning on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wednesday it was weaker at HK$7.7624/34, closer to its pegged   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 exchange rate of HK$7.80 per greenback, but still stubbornly on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the peg's stronger side.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Dealers said demand for Hong Kong dollars for upcoming large\par share issues was adding to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength.\par     The HKMA's moves were the latest in a string of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 since a highly unusual strengthening of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar in   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 late September which saw it rise to nearly HK$7.70 per U.S.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The HKMA has said it will not formally set a limit on how   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strong it will allow the Hong Kong dollar to get, but it is   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 committed to preventing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from weakening below the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HK$7.80 per dollar mark.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers said the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  faces a key resistance   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 barrier at 7.77. Since the Hong Kong dollar strengthened in late   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September, the spot rate has made several attempts to break above   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 that level but has repeatedly failed.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The discount on the one-year Hong Kong dollar forwards,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reflecting some traders perceptions of the unit's appreciation   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 over the next year, widened to 445/425 pips by mid-morning, from   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 395/375 late on Tuesday.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                     Morning        Previous Close\par                     At 0235 GMT    At 0900 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT        7.7629/39      7.7633/34\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month     -183 / -176    -175 / -170\par     Six-month       -320 / -310    -290 / -280\par     One-year        -445 / -425    -395 / -375\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight       0.00 / 0.00    0.01 / 0.02\par     Three-month     0.09 / 0.21    0.18 / 0.21\par     Six-month       0.34 / 0.46    0.42 / 0.45\par     One-year        0.93 / 1.06    1.02 / 1.05\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031203dzc3000mb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
