\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dlr Mkts Late: HK Dlr Gains Capped As HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 424 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2003\par 09:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar strengthened further Wednesday, but its gains were capped around HK$7.76 after fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was quoted at HK$7.7620, compared with HK$7.7637 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The city's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market late Tuesday and early Wednesday, selling a total of HK$730 million to curb the local unit's rise against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said they believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place when the local unit was close to HK$7.76, a target level implied by the HKMA's recent moves.  \par \par \uc2 While the sale kept the Hong Kong dollar's gains capped at HK$7.76, it is unlikely to push the local unit much lower, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "Given the ongoing foreign interest in local equities, which may be further boosted by upcoming IPOs, fund inflows will provide firm support for the Hong Kong dollar," one trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA's injections added further liquidity into an already flush interbank market, pushing Hong Kong interbank offered rates lower.  \par \par \uc2 The one-month Hibor was quoted at 0.09%, down from 0.11% Tuesday. The 12-month Hibor was quoted at 1.02%, compared with 1.05% previously.  \par \par \uc2 The drop in Hibors stretched the interest rate gap between the Hong Kong dollar and the U.S. dollar, which had the effect of further widening the discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards.  \par \par \uc2 The one-year contract was quoted at 460-440 below the spot rate, compared with 400-390 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong Exchange Fund note yields fell slightly in thin activity. The 10-year bond was quoted at 4.58%, compared with 4.61% Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Still, traders expect recent signs of economic revival and equity strength to keep bond yields on an upward bias, especially among long-dated issues.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                   Latest        Late Tuesday \par Overnight Hibor    0.02%          0.02% \par 1-mo Hibor         0.09%          0.11% \par 3-mo Hibor         0.19%          0.20% \par 1-yr Hibor         1.02%          1.05% \par USD/HKD Spot       HK$7.7620      HK$7.7637 \par 6-mo HKD Fwd       -320 to -313   -290 to -282 \par 1-yr HKD Fwd       -460 to -440   -400 to -390 \par  \par 4.32% EF Note Due Dec. 2, 2013: \par  \par    Price: 98.34 Vs 98.13 \par    Yield: 4.58% Vs 4.61% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Raymond Tsoi, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; raymond.tsoi@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by John Viljoen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1053 4178  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031203dzc30009h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
