\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA Sells HK$730M In Two Transactions To Weaken HK Dlr  \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2003\par 01:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets late Tuesday and early Wednesday, selling a total of HK$730 million to weaken the Hong Kong dollar's gains against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 After the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.S. dollar was quoted at HK$7.7627, down slightly from HK$7.7637 late Tuesday Hong Kong time.  \par \par \uc2 "There was some reaction, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still within its trading range," a trader said.  \par \par \uc2 It wasn't immediately apparent how much the Hong Kong dollar had moved during London and New York trading hours, but the HKMA has in the past \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the U.S. dollar drops below the HK$7.76 level.  \par \par \uc2 In recent days, the Hong Kong dollar has undergone another round of strengthening in response to a better-than-expected performance of the local economy in the third quarter, when gross domestic product grew 4% on year.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA typically doesn't comment on its market actions, but it does provide data on its transactions to financial data systems. Those show that it sold HK$621 million and HK$109 million in two separate transactions, equivalent to buying about US$94 million.  \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar's spot exchange rate has been stronger than its peg rate of HK$7.80 to the U.S. dollar since late September, an unusual situation driven by a combination of strong foreign investor interest in Hong Kong's stock and property markets, and speculation on the possible appreciation of the Chinese yuan, using the Hong Kong dollar as a proxy.  \par \par \uc2 -By Andrew Batson, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; andrew.batson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Andrew Bullard  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031203dzc30000x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
