\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dlr Mkts Late: HK Dlr A Tad Lower But Well Supported  \b0\par\par\uc2 467 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2003\par 09:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar weakened slightly Tuesday in thin trade, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's downside is likely to be limited given recent strong domestic product data and continued strength in the local share market, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was quoted at HK$7.7637, compared with HK$7.7615 late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said they expect strong support for the Hong Kong dollar at 7.77.  \par \par \uc2 "Given the growing signs of economic revival, strong performance of local shares and a series of upcoming IPOs, foreign funds are likely to remain attracted to the Hong Kong market," a trader said. "Such ongoing fund inflows will keep the Hong Kong dollar well supported."  \par \par \uc2 Traders, however, think the upside for the local unit is also well contained, expecting resistance around HK$7.76, a level established by the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Excess interbank liquidity persisted, keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank offered rates close to historical lows.  \par \par \uc2 The one-month Hibor was quoted at 0.11%, down from 0.12% Monday. The 12-month Hibor was quoted at 1.05%, compared with 1.07% previously.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong dollar forwards remained at a deep discount as the large interbank surplus kept Hong Kong dollar interest rates well below those of the U.S. The one-year contract was quoted at 400-390 below the spot rate, compared with 380-360 Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Short-dated Hong Kong Exchange Fund note yields eased modestly given the low Hibors. The two-year EF note was quoted at 1.64%, compared with 1.66% Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Long-maturity EF note yields, by contrast, rose after a stronger U.S. Institute for Supply Management manufacturing index, which showed the most robust activity in two decades last month.  \par \par \uc2 The private Institute for Supply Management said Monday its November index of manufacturing activity came in at 62.8, up from 57 for October. The data also provide solid evidence of an improving manufacturing jobs picture, as the ISM's employment index climbed to 51 from 47.7.  \par \par \uc2 The 10-year EF note was quoted at 4.61%, up from 4.59% Monday.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                   Latest        Late Monday \par Overnight Hibor    0.02%          0.02% \par 1-mo Hibor         0.11%          0.12% \par 3-mo Hibor         0.20%          0.23% \par 1-yr Hibor         1.05%          1.07% \par USD/HKD Spot       HK$7.7637      HK$7.7615 \par 6-mo HKD Fwd       -290 to -282   -291 to -281 \par 1-yr HKD Fwd       -400 to -390   -380 to -360 \par  \par 4.32% EF Note Due Dec. 2, 2013: \par  \par    Price: 98.13 Vs 98.28 \par    Yield: 4.61% Vs 4.59% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Raymond Tsoi, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; raymond.tsoi@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by John Viljoen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1053 4178  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031202dzc2000ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
