\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dlr Mkts Late: Hibors A Tad Higher On Month-End Demand  \b0\par\par\uc2 446 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2003\par 09:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank offered rates rose slightly Wednesday due to month-end demand and continued stability in the Hong Kong dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The one-month Hibor was quoted at 0.13%, compared with 0.12% Tuesday. The 12-month Hibor was quoted at 1.06%, up from 1.05% previously.  \par \par \uc2 "The month-end borrowing needs boosted Hibors slightly, but the volume was rather thin," a trader noted.  \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar remained stable in a narrow range between HK$7.7600 to HK$7.7700, traders said, suggesting that further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be necessary. This spurred some position adjustments, which kept the upward pressure on Hibors.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was quoted at HK$7.7670, compared with HK$7.7680 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 In line with the local unit's stability in the spot market, Hong Kong dollar forwards spent the day in a narrow trading band.  \par \par \uc2 The one-year contract was quoted at 330-310 below the spot rate, unchanged from Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Although most traders said they expect forwards to remain at deep discounts in the near term, given the surplus funds in the interbank market, they consider the room for further widening of the discount to be limited.  \par \par \uc2 "As the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is finally stabilizing after recent aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the HKMA, there is nothing else to justify further sharp declines in forwards," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong Exchange Fund Note yields dropped slightly, led by long-dated issues, after a spike Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The 10-year EF note was quoted at 4.42%, compared with 4.46% Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "After the brief yield rise Tuesday, investors are gradually returning to the market as liquidity is still flush, leaving them with few alternatives to park their surplus funds" the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The Federal Reserve's recent comments pointing to a low inflation risk also implied an accommodative interest rate policy will stay intact for the months to come. This also helped boost demand for bonds, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                   Latest        Late Tuesday \par Overnight Hibor    0.01%          0.01% \par 1-mo Hibor         0.13%          0.12% \par 3-mo Hibor         0.27%          0.25% \par 1-yr Hibor         1.06%          1.05% \par USD/HKD Spot       HK$7.7670      HK$7.7680 \par 6-mo HKD Fwd       -275 to -255   -275 to -270 \par 1-yr HKD Fwd       -330 to -310   -330 to -310 \par  \par 3.73% EF Note Due June 5, 2013: \par  \par    Price: 99.63 Vs 99.33 \par    Yield: 4.42% Vs 4.46% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Raymond Tsoi, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; raymond.tsoi@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by John Viljoen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1053 4178  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031126dzbq000d6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
