\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dlr Mkts Late: US Dollar Steadies Above HK$7.76  \b0\par\par\uc2 477 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2003\par 09:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar weakened against the U.S. dollar Friday, as markets digested the government's commitment to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening too far from its peg rate.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was quoted around HK$7.7610 Friday, up from HK$7.7595 Thursday. In line with the weaker spot rate, the discount on the one-year Hong Kong dollar forward contract also narrowed, to 435 to 415, from 450 to 430 previously.  \par \par \uc2 "Recently, one of the most important factors in the market is the attitude of the government to the spot rate," a trader said. "The government has given strong signals to the market."  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong Financial Secretary Henry Tang Thursday reiterated the government's commitment to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar market if necessary to prevent volatility.  \par \par \uc2 Over the past two weeks, the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold about HK$7.27 billion, buying more than US$930 million in a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions. Those have usually been timed when the U.S. dollar dropped below HK$7.76.  \par \par \uc2 However, market participants don't expect the spot rate to return to the peg rate of HK$7.80 to the U.S. dollar in the short term, as the local stock market continues to attract foreign investment.  \par \par \uc2 There was some talk the rising spot rate may have been influenced by frightened investors repatriating funds after Thursday's terrorist attacks in Istanbul, though the relatively small movement in the rate Friday argued against it.  \par \par \uc2 "If it's true, the amount of money is quite limited," another trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The terrorist attacks did prompt some flight-to-quality buying of U.S. Treasurys, which in turn caused yields on Hong Kong Exchange Fund notes to drop slightly.  \par \par \uc2 The yield on the two-year EF note was quoted at 1.35%, from 1.37% Thursday, while that on the 10-year EF note fell to 4.22% from 4.24% previously.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong interbank offered rates remained at very low levels. The one-year Hibor fell to 0.87% from 0.90% Thursday, though the three-month Hibor was unchanged at 0.16%.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                   Latest        Late Thursday \par Overnight Hibor   0.003%        0.005% \par 1-mo Hibor        0.05%         0.04% \par 3-mo Hibor        0.16%         0.16% \par 1-yr Hibor        0.87%         0.90% \par USD/HKD Spot      HK$7.7610     HK$7.7595 \par 6-mo HKD Fwd      -315 to -305  -325 to -315 \par 1-yr HKD Fwd      -435 to -415  -450 to -430 \par  \par 3.73% EF Note Due Jun. 5, 2013: \par  \par    Price: 96.55 Vs 96.34 \par    Yield: 4.22% Vs 4.24% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Andrew Batson, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; andrew.batson@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Andrew Bullard  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1053 4178  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031121dzbl000ia\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
