\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar drifts lower despite HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2003\par 05:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Nov 20 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar eased\par only marginally on Thursday morning despite persistent\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) to\par weaken the local unit, which has strengthened away from the peg\par since September.\par     Dealers said the HKMA's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were becoming less\par effective due to the weakness of the U.S. dollar and\par profit-taking from investors whenever the local unit edged\par lower against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The U.S. dollar was softer on Thursday on geopolitical\par concerns and worries about the fallout from Washington's plans\par to impose import quotas on Chinese textiles.\par     "There is still heavy selling in the U.S. dollar in the\par market. I believe some are short term speculative trades, and\par at the same time some banks continue to unwind their long USD\par positions," said a dealer from a local bank.\par     Some banks have accumulated a lot of U.S.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollars against\par the local unit in arbitrage trades in the past, a dealer from a\par European bank said. As the U.S. dollar weakens, many are\par selling U.S. dollars to liquidate their positions.\par  \par     At 0345 GMT, the Hong Kong dollar        was trading at\par 7.7585/95, compared with 7.7556/66 at 0845 GMT on Wednesday.\par     The HKMA, the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , has\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market seven times so far this week and\par bought a total of US$337 million.\par     The HKMA is obligated to defend the Hong Kong dollar from\par weakening below its HK$7.80 peg with the U.S. dollar but has no\par mandate to stop it from strengthening above that level.\par     After the latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday, the aggregate\par balance -- a key measure of interbank liquidity -- will rise to\par HK$11.534 billion on Friday.\par     A jump in the aggregate balance will put further pressure\par on already low interbank rates and force the discount on Hong\par Kong dollar forwards even wider.\par     The discount on one-year Hong Kong dollar forwards\par was trading at around 485/465 pips versus 480/460 pips late on\par Wednesday.\par     "After the one-year forwards broke the technical support of\par -400 pips, the next resistance will be at -500 pips," one\par trader said.\par                     Morning       Previous Close\par                     At 0345 GMT   At 0925 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT        7.7585/95     7.7558/64\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month     -200 / -190   -200 / -195\par     Six-month       -350 / -335   -355 / -345\par     One-year        -485 / -465   -480 / -460\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight      0.001 / 0.001 0.001 / 0.001\par     Three-month     0.10 / 0.12   0.07 / 0.10\par     Six-month       0.25 / 0.28   0.25 / 0.31\par     One-year        0.78 / 0.83   0.75 / 0.83\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Live quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Reuters contributor page .\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031120dzbk001bg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
