\par\par \b \uc2 PRESS DIGEST - HONG KONG - Nov 20.  \b0\par\par\uc2 533 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2003\par 02:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, November 20 (Reuters) - These are some of the leading stories in Hong Kong newspapers on Thursday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG ECONOMIC TIMES  \par \par \uc2 - Major political parties will stand behind a motion to be forwarded by the Democrats next week to block the controversial mega-project for West Kowloon cultural development, which the government is offering under a single contract.  \par \par \uc2 - Mainland China says the reform by opening the yuan's banking service market will be gradual and progressive, and that Hong Kong's yuan business will not hurt stability.  \par \par \uc2 APPLE DAILY  \par \par \uc2 - The Hang Seng Index fell below the 12,000 mark after textiles counters fell on the news about US tariffs announced for Chinese garment items.  \par \par \uc2 MING PAO DAILY NEWS  \par \par \uc2 - An outbreak of the Norwalk virus is expected to extend its effects on Hong Kong Island over the next few months, experts say. The stomach-attacking virus has hit some 400 people.  \par \par \uc2 - A People's Bank of China spokesman quoted by Xinhua says credit card issuers will limit usage of their cards by travellers to Hong Kong to certain authorised merchants.  \par \par \uc2 SOUTH CHINA MORNING POST  \par \par \uc2 - Interest in the U.S. equity market among Hong Kong investors is slowly returning to the pre-September 11 level, according to Charles Schwab (Hong Kong).  \par \par \uc2 - Chief Executive Tung Chee-hwa has appointed a senior civil servant to head the Audit Commission, raising public concerns over the watchdog's independence on doing external audit on the government.  \par \par \uc2 THE STANDARD  \par \par \uc2 - Talks between Hong Kong and Australia to agree on a new air pact that would have increased passenger capacity on routes between Hong Kong, Australia, Europe and the U.S. have collapsed in Canberra.  \par \par \uc2 - Moody's Investors Service expects Hong Kong's first real estate investment trusts to be launched next year, with the Housing Authority likely to be one fo the front-runners.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG ECONOMIC JOURNAL  \par \par \uc2 - The government has suspended the development proposal for the prime Tamar site in Central indefinitely due to budgetary concerns after SARS.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  DAILY NEWS  \par \par \uc2 - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times yesterday to suppress the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with US dollar purchases. The aggregate balance in the interbank market will rise over the HK$10 billion mark.  \par \par \uc2 SING PAO  \par \par \uc2 - Textiles manufacturers in Hong Kong believe the new import quotas by imposed by the U.S. on certain mainland products would not have a huge impact because the items affected only represent a small percentage of the total volume. They also see the move as a political one.  \par \par \uc2 WEN WEI PO  \par \par \uc2 - Hong Kong's credit card receivables write-off ratio fell to single-digit in the third quarter - the lowest since the first quarter 2002. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said charge-off fell to 9.85 percent at HK$1.33 billion for the quarter.  \par \par \uc2 TA KUNG PAO  \par \par \uc2 - Hutchison Whampoa (0013.HK) has enlarged the size of its current bond sale to US$5 billion from US$3 billion. Sources say total subscription now equals HK$12 billion and prices for the tranches will be set on Wednesday night in New York.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031120dzbk00041\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\