\par\par \b \uc2 HK Fincl Secy:  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Will Continue If Needed  \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2003\par 09:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  Financial Secretary Henry Tang said the government won't hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if needed.  \par \par \uc2 "If necessary, we will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Tang told reporters Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Tang said the recent strength of the local unit reflects rising confidence in the city's economy.  \par \par \uc2 The strong demand for the Hong Kong dollar was also due to diminishing concerns that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be devalued, Tang added. However, "there is no reason at all to change the (U.S. dollar) peg."  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong dollar forwards, a barometer of the level of confidence in the city's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, mostly traded at a premium to the spot market in recent years, as the city faced a prolonged period of economic weakness marked by rising unemployment and deepening deflation.  \par \par \uc2 But market sentiment started to turn around as Hong Kong's economy began showing signs of recovery, boosted by a revival in tourism and business opportunities from its trade pact with China.  \par \par \uc2 In late September, heavy selling of the U.S. dollar against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  triggered a sharp rise of the Hong Kong dollar above the HK$7.80 peg rate, pushing the one-year forwards to trade at a discount from a premium.  \par \par \uc2 The slide of the U.S. dollar prompted a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been fighting to preserve the Hong Kong dollar peg. In the past two weeks, the HKMA bought US$937 million in the spot market.  \par \par \uc2 But the HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had little effect on the U.S. dollar, barely keeping it around 7.76, which is believed to be the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target level.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the strength of the local unit to persist in the near term as the recovering economy and local equities continue to attract foreign funds.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar's general slide against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the intensifying trade dispute between the U.S. and China will also keep upward pressure on the Hong Kong dollar.  \par \par \uc2 -By Raymond Tsoi, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; raymond.tsoi@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -Edited by Sharon Buan \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031120dzbk000f5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
