\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr remains firm despite HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2003\par 11:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Nov 19 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  twice on Wednesday to try to\par stabilise the local unit's strength but it remained stubbornly\par strong against the U.S. dollar, to which it is pegged.\par     At 0845 GMT, the Hong Kong dollar        was trading at\par 7.7556/66 to the dollar, compared with 7.7572 at 1702 GMT on\par Tuesday.\par     "If the rate deviates so much from 7.8 that it makes market\par players or citizens doubt this exchange rate system, I will\par definitely take action," HKMA's chief executive Joseph Yam said\par to reporters in Beijing.\par     The HKMA is obligated to defend the Hong Kong dollar from\par weakening below its HK$7.80 peg with the U.S. dollar but has no\par mandate to stop it from strengthening above that level.\par     The HKMA, the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , sold a total\par of HK$1.163 million (US$150 million) on Wednesday.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  This is the\par fifth time in two days that the HKMA has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market\par according to information it publishes daily on Reuters screens\par  .\par  \par     It also sold a total of HK$1.318 billion (US$170 million) on\par Tuesday during London and New York trading hours.\par     As a result, the aggregate balance, a key measure of\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 interbank liquidity, will increase to HK$11.402 billion on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Friday. This will push local interbank rates lower and force the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards even wider.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "People had accumulated a lot of U.S. dollars against the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 local unit in arbitrage trades in the past. As the U.S. dollar   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 weakens, those who have burnt their figures are rushing to sell   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. dollars to liquidate their positions," said a dealer from a   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French bank.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some dealers said banks in Hong Kong had become cautious   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 about the size of their short term U.S. dollar holdings due to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the greenback's recent weakness and the volatility of the local   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 unit, which has been strengthening since late September.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think many banks in Hong Kong have given instructions to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 traders to limit the size of U.S. dollar holdings to control   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk," said another dealer from a European bank.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar fell against the euro on Wednesday after   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Washington said it would impose import quotas on Chinese   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 textiles, fuelling fears of protectionism that could undermine   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the U.S. economic recovery.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Dealers also said investors were reluctant to buy U.S.\par dollars against the local unit in arbitrage.\par     "As the interest rate differential between U.S. dollar and\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong dollar is only one percentage point, there is in fact   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 not much of an incentive for people to buy U.S. dollar," one   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dealer said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The discount on one-year Hong Kong dollar forwards   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 broke key support at 400 pips and deepened to a fresh low of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 480/460 pips by late afternoon versus 385 pips late on Tuesday.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Meanwhile, the one-year interbank rate fell to 0.75-0.83\par percent from 0.87-0.93 percent on Tuesday.\par                     Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                     At 0925 GMT   At 0200 GMT   At 0843 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT        7.7558/64     7.7562/68     7.7610/12\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month     -200 / -195   -200 / -193   -185 / -180\par     Six-month       -355 / -345   -345 / -335   -300 / -290\par     One-year        -480 / -460   -460 / -440   -390 / -370\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight      0.001 / 0.001 0.001 / 0.001 0.001 / 0.005\par     Three-month     0.07 / 0.10   0.09 / 0.11   0.14 / 0.18\par     Six-month       0.25 / 0.31   0.23 / 0.25   0.37 / 0.42\par     One-year        0.75 / 0.83   0.75 / 0.77   0.87 / 0.93\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031119dzbj0028n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
