\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA Sells Additional HK$82 Mln In Latest  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 150 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2003\par 11:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold an additional HK$82 million, buying approximately US$10 million, in its third \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the day Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The sale brings the HKMA's total \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the day to HK$1.24 billion, and comes after three transactions overnight Tuesday totaling HK$1.32 billion. All were aimed at weakening the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Over the past week and a half, the HKMA has been selling Hong Kong dollars and buying U.S. dollars when the U.S. dollar dips below the HK$7.76 level. However, the latest sale pushed the rate up only marginally to HK$7.7565, from HK$7.7555 earlier in the day.  \par \par \uc2 -By Andrew Batson, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; andrew.batson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Andrew Bullard  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031119dzbj000ma\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
