\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dlr Mkts Late: HK Dlr Stronger On Global US Dlr Sales  \b0\par\par\uc2 504 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2003\par 09:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar strengthened in the spot and forwards markets Wednesday, in response to heavy selling of the U.S. dollar against major global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was quoted around HK$7.7555, down from HK$7.7610 Tuesday. The benchmark one-year Hong Kong dollar forward was quoted at 480 to 460 below the spot rate, much deeper than the 390 to 375 discount Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "We see some relocation of money from the U.S. into higher yielding markets," a trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The drop in the spot rate below the HK$7.76 level triggered another round of overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The HKMA sold a total of HK$1.32 billion in three transactions, buying U.S. dollars at an exchange rate estimated around HK$7.7530. The HKMA has been active in the market in the past week, usually moving when the U.S. dollar falls below HK$7.76.  \par \par \uc2 The effectiveness of the HKMA's latest \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to be waning, as the U.S. dollar didn't move back above HK$7.76. Still, traders suggested the U.S. dollar would have traded even weaker against the Hong Kong dollar without them.  \par \par \uc2 "Once they (the HKMA) start taking action, they can't stop. If they did, the spot rate would really slide," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The latest sale by the HKMA added further liquidity to an interbank market already swimming in surplus cash, helping to further push down Hong Kong interbank offered rates.  \par \par \uc2 The three-month Hibor fell to 0.13%, from 0.19% Tuesday, while the one-year Hibor dropped to 0.87%, from 0.93% previously.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said rates were likely to keep falling until funds start moving out of Hong Kong. The strong performance of the local stock market has attracted many investors, while others are speculating on an appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Yields on Hong Kong exchange fund notes fell, after the U.S. issued data showing slow inflation, and an official from the Federal Reserve repeated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's disinclination to raise U.S. interest rates in the short term.  \par \par \uc2 The yield on the two-year EF note was quoted at 1.24%, from 1.36% Tuesday, while the 10-year note was down to 4.15%, from 4.26% previously.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                   Latest        Late Tuesday \par Overnight Hibor   0.005%        0.005% \par 1-mo Hibor        0.03%         0.06% \par 3-mo Hibor        0.13%         0.19% \par 1-yr Hibor        0.87%         0.93% \par USD/HKD Spot      HK$7.7555     HK$7.7610 \par 6-mo HKD Fwd      -345 to -335  -300 to -290 \par 1-yr HKD Fwd      -480 to -460  -390 to -375 \par  \par 3.73% EF Note Due Jun. 5, 2013: \par  \par    Price: 97.08 Vs 96.33 \par    Yield: 4.15% Vs 4.26% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Andrew Batson, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; andrew.batson@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Andrew Bullard  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1053 4178  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031119dzbj000ey\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
