\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA Moves To Curb HK Dollar Rise Becoming Less Effective  \b0\par\par\uc2 551 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2003\par 05:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market again late Tuesday in a bid to prevent the U.S. dollar from weakening against the local unit, but the effectiveness of the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves appears to be waning.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA doesn't normally comment on its market activities, but does provide information on its transactions to financial data systems, which show it sold HK$1,318 million, equivalent to buying around US$170 million.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA sold about HK$4.66 billion last week.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the U.S. dollar's general slide against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  led to a fall in the U.S. dollar against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar overnight, and prompted three rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the HKMA. A money trader estimated the transactions were executed at an average exchange rate of HK$7.7530.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA's latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, hasn't been entirely effective in curbing the appreciation of the Hong Kong dollar: the U.S. dollar was being quoted at HK$7.7555 Wednesday morning, lower than its level of HK$7.7610 Tuesday afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 The belief in the market is that the HKMA is aiming to keep the U.S. dollar from dipping much below HK$7.76.  \par \par \uc2 "Market sentiment is against the U.S. dollar, given its general slide against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the money trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Traders were also concerned an intensifying trade dispute between the U.S. and mainland China could lead to a resurgence in political pressure for a yuan revaluation.  \par \par \uc2 Since the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't freely tradable, market participants often use the Hong Kong dollar as a proxy for the yuan given the close economic relationship between the territory and mainland China, even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have no real ties.  \par \par \uc2 "Despite the HKMA's clear commitment to keeping the peg, and significantly higher U.S. dollar interest rates than Hong Kong dollar interest rates, market participants remain reluctant to long the U.S. dollar," the trader noted.  \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar strayed from the HK$7.80 peg rate Sept. 22, when there was heavy selling of the U.S. dollar against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The U.S. dollar was quoted as low as HK$7.71 in the immediate aftermath, but then rebounded to around HK$7.77 before coming under selling pressure again recently.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA's repeated sales of Hong Kong dollars have flooded the interbank market with surplus funds. The aggregate balance, a key measure of interbank surplus liquidity, will rise to over HK$10 billion Thursday when the HKMA's latest transactions settle.  \par \par \uc2 The excess liquidity has depressed Hong Kong interest rates and pushed the discounts on Hong Kong dollar forwards to their deepest levels since forwards moved from a premium to a discount late September.  \par \par \uc2 The one-year forward was quoted at a discount of 450-440 to the spot rate Wednesday morning, compared with a discount of 390-375 Tuesday afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 "Forwards are likely to remain at a deep discount unless there are major outflows, but that seems unlikely in the near term," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Raymond Tsoi, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; raymond.tsoi@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Andrew Bullard  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031119dzbj00051\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
