\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr range trades, forwards discount widens.   \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2003\par 11:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Nov 17 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar was\par rangebound on Monday on cautious sentiment after a series of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) last\par week.\par     The local unit shuffled between 7.7580-7.76 for most of the\par day. It was trading at 7.7590 to the dollar at 0925 GMT,\par compared with 7.7578/98 at 0917 GMT on Friday.\par     "We don't know if the HKMA will step into the market again.\par So investors are more cautious," a dealer at a European bank\par said, explaining the range trading.\par     The HKMA, the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , bought\par US$600 million last week against the HK dollar to show its\par commitment to exchange rate stability. The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par been strengthening over recent weeks.\par     The aggregate balance, a key measure of interbank\par liquidity, will expand to HK$8.966 billion on Tuesday -- the\par highest level since November 1998. High liquidity pushes\par interbank rates down.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The government is deliberately keeping the Hong Kong\par interbank rates low to encourage banks to buy U.S. dollars\par against the local units in arbitrage. A long time ago, say in\par 1987, such arbitrage was seen lucrative as U.S. interest rates\par were notably higher than the Hong Kong counterparts. But now,\par as the U.S. interest rates are so low, investors see artibrage\par as less attractive," another dealer said.\par     The interest rate differential between the Hong Kong dollar\par and the U.S. dollar was around one full percentage point at\par present, the dealer added.\par  \par     He expected the spot rate to move between 7.75-7.77 to the\par dollar in the near term.\par     Traders see a risk of further HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the near\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 term, which will push local interbank rates down further -   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 short term rates are already close to zero - and widen the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One-year Hong Kong dollar forwards were trading around   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -400/-380 pips by late afternoon, down from -350/-360 late on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Friday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One dealer at a French bank said the next target for the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 forwards will be at -450 pips.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031117dzbh002a8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
