\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr remains above peg, further HKMA action eyed.   \b0\par\par\uc2 444 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2003\par 05:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Nov 17 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar remained\par well above its pegged exchange rate of 7.80 to the U.S. dollar on\par Monday morning despite several \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) last week to stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "There is still a lot of selling pressure on the U.S. dollar\par and it is pushed down as soon as it tries to move ahead," said a\par dealer at a local bank.\par     The local unit        was trading at 7.7590 to the dollar at\par 0332 GMT, compared with 7.7570/80 in early trade and 7.7578/98 at\par 0917 GMT on Friday.\par  \par     Another dealer said there was some short term speculative\par activity although strong resistance remained at 7.77.\par     The HKMA, the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , bought\par US$600 million last week against the HK dollar to show its\par commitment to exchange rate stability.\par     The aggregate balance, a key measure of interbank liquidity,\par will expand to HK$8.966 billion on Tuesday -- the highest level\par since November 1998.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders see a risk of further HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the near\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 term, which will lead local interbank rates even lower - short   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 term rates are already close to zero - and to a further widening   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of the discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     One-year Hong Kong dollar forwards were trading at -395/-375\par pips in morning trade, down from -360/-350 pips late on Friday.\par     Some traders expected resistance at -400 pips, with the next\par target at -420 to -450 pips.\par     The one-year local rate was quoted at 0.88-0.90 versus\par 0.97-1.02 percent, another dealer from a local bank said.\par     Meanwhile, Hong Kong's latest unemployment rate is set to be\par released on Monday afternoon.\par     A Reuters poll of 10 economists forecast the unemployment\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rate to slip to 8.1 percent in the three months to end-October   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 compared with 8.3 percent in the July-to-September period, helped   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 by an economic recovery.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                 Morning       Previous Close\par                     At 0332 GMT   At 0915 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT        7.7590/93     7.7570/81\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month     -190 / -180   -184 / -179\par     Six-month       -310 / -300   -296 / -286\par     One-year        -395 / -375   -360 / -350\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight      0.005 / 0.007  0.01 / 0.06\par     Three-month     0.12 / 0.15   0.12 / 0.24\par     Six-month       0.35 / 0.38   0.34 / 0.46\par     One-year        0.88 / 0.90   0.75 / 1.00\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031117dzbh000pz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
