\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA Sells HK$776 Mln In Latest Move To Weaken HK Dlr  \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2003\par 09:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday sold HK$776 million into the market in its latest move to stem the strengthening of the Hong Kong dollar.  \par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said Friday's sale, the latest in a series of moves by the HKMA this week, took place when the U.S. dollar was quoted around HK$7.7575.  \par \par \uc2 The sales this week have convinced the market the HKMA won't permit the U.S. dollar to fall below the HK$7.76 level.  \par \par \uc2 "7.76 is already the alert level for the HKMA. Each time we break this level, they come in and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA has sold \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars into the market every day this week, in its most active series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since late September, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's exchange rate has been stronger than the peg rate of HK$7.80 to the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The latest transaction brings the HKMA's total \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week to about HK$4.7 billion, or around US$600 million.  \par \par \uc2 The repeated injections of cash into the system have pushed down interest rates, already extremely low, and demonstrated the HKMA's commitment to the city's 20-year-old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg.  \par \par \uc2 But as the repeated strengthening of the Hong Kong dollar shows, traders remain reluctant to buy the U.S. dollar, given its weakness against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "This afternoon there wasn't enough liquidity, and a few traders were able to push the rate from 7.7620 to as low as 7.7520 in just a minute," the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said. "So the HKMA move was widely expected by traders."  \par \par \uc2 The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, wasn't able to keep the U.S. dollar above the HK$7.76 level. Late Friday afternoon, after the HKMA sale, the U.S. dollar was quoted around HK$7.7580, compared with HK$7.7620 earlier in the day.  \par \par \uc2 -By Andrew Batson, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; andrew.batson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Andrew Bullard  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031114dzbe000ke\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
