\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dlr Mkts Late: HK$ Eases After HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  Again  \b0\par\par\uc2 462 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2003\par 09:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar weakened further Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the market to strengthen the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The HKMA has shown a very aggressive stance in recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," one trader said. "It has indicated clearly excessive strength of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be tolerated."  \par \par \uc2 The quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold an additional HK$777 million Thursday to push up the U.S. dollar, after having injected over HK$2.3 billion in the previous three days.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar rose gradually after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and was quoted at HK$7.7665 late Thursday, up from HK$7.7630 Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the HKMA could sell the local unit again in coming weeks to help the U.S. dollar gradually move back toward the HK$7.80 peg rate.  \par \par \uc2 "Potential \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the HKMA may deter traders from selling the U.S. dollar, which will keep it well supported around HK$7.760 in the near term," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Discounts on Hong Kong dollar forwards narrowed following the HKMA's move, which was seen as a strong signal the city's U.S. dollar peg will be kept intact over the long term.  \par \par \uc2 The one-year contract was quoted at a discount of 320-300 to the spot rate, compared with 370-350 Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Long-dated Hong Kong interbank offered rates edged higher amid stronger borrowing interest from foreign banks, as the rates were considered cheap relative to comparable U.S. dollar London interbank offered rates.  \par \par \uc2 The one-year Hibor was quoted at 1.14%, up from 1.08% Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "Foreign banks are quite keen to borrow longer term funds, especially the one year," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 If there is little chance of the Hong Kong dollar appreciating, the one-year Hibor can't justify trading at more than 40 basis points below the one-year U.S. dollar Libor, traders said, adding that an upward bias is therefore likely to persist.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong Exchange Fund note yields barely moved. The yield on the 10-year bond was 4.50%, the same as Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                   Latest        Late Wednesday \par Overnight Hibor   0.02%            0.02% \par 1-mo Hibor        0.05%            0.05% \par 3-mo Hibor        0.30%            0.29% \par 1-yr Hibor        1.14%            1.08% \par USD/HKD Spot      HK$7.7665        HK$7.7630 \par 6-mo HKD Fwd      -260 t0 -250     -290 to -280 \par 1-yr HKD Fwd      -320 to -300     -370 to -350 \par  \par 3.73% EF Note Due Jun. 5, 2013: \par  \par    Price: 94.45 Vs 94.43 \par    Yield: 4.50% Vs 4.50% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Raymond Tsoi, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; raymond.tsoi@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Andrew Bullard  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031113dzbd000gm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
