\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr weakens further after HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2003\par 05:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Nov 12 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar weakened\par against the U.S. dollar on Thursday after the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) bought another US$100 million against the local\par unit, in a further attempt to stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     This is the fifth time since late on Monday that the\par territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market.\par The HKMA has now bought a total of US$400 million this week,\par according to information it publishes daily on Reuters screens\par  .\par     As a result, the aggregate balance, a key measure of\par interbank liquidity, will further expand to HK$7.414 billion on\par November 17 from HK$5.851 billion on Thursday.\par     "It's very clear that the HKMA is trying to maintain the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg but it is unwilling to push the Hong Kong dollar any\par higher than that," said a dealer at a local bank.\par     The HKMA is obligated to defend the Hong Kong dollar from\par weakening below its HK$7.80 peg with the U.S.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar but has no\par mandate to stop it from strengthening above that level.\par  \par     The local unit was trading at 7.7663/73 at 0413 GMT, versus\par 7.7640 at 0921 GMT on Wednesday.\par     "The downside is limited in the spot market because of the\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 presence of the HKMA, which appears determined to push the value   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of the Hong Kong dollar to 7.80," another dealer from a Japanese   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 bank.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards narrowed on short\par covering, dealers said.\par     "There has been some short covering after the one-year\par contracts deepened to -380 pips on Wednesday," one dealer said.\par     One-year forwards          were trading around -330/-310\par pips, compared with -365/-355 pips late on Wednesday.\par     The market is looking ahead to U.S. jobless claims figures\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 due later in the day and U.S. industrial production and retail   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 sales data on Friday. U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greenspan will also be speaking on Friday.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0425 GMT   At 0904 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7663/73     7.7635/36\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -180 / -170   -183 / -178\par     Six-month        -270 / -260   -292 / -282\par     One-year         -330 / -310   -365 / -355\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight        0.01 / 0.01   0.01 / 0.02\par     Three-month      0.20 / 0.22   0.20 / 0.23\par     Six-month        0.43 / 0.47   0.40 / 0.45\par     One-year         1.05 / 1.08   1.02 / 1.05\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par Reuters contributor page .\par     (US$=HK$7.8).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031113dzbd000xd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
