\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dlr Mkts Late: HK Dlr Dn After Fresh HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 436 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2003\par 09:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar weakened Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market for a third day in a row, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar rose to HK$7.7630, compared with HK$7.7539 Tuesday afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA sold HK$776 million Wednesday, and bought about US$100 million to further suppress the local unit's recent rise against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The sale came as the U.S. dollar was already rebounding following the HKMA's previous injections totaling HK$1.55 billion.  \par \par \uc2 "The aggressive moves from the HKMA in recent days showed it will not tolerate big deviation from the HK$7.80 U.S. dollar peg rate," a money trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA's injections of over HK$2.3 billion since Monday have increased liquidity in an already flush interbank market, leading to further declines in Hong Kong interbank offered rates, which have been trading around historical lows.  \par \par \uc2 The one-month Hibor was quoted at 0.05%, down from 0.10% Tuesday. The 12-month Hibor was quoted at 1.08%, down from 1.10% previously.  \par \par \uc2 The drop in Hibors fueled demand for short-dated Hong Kong Exchange Fund papers, as investors shifted funds away from short-term interbank deposits to achieve higher returns.  \par \par \uc2 The 12-month EF bill was quoted at 0.60%, compared with 0.72% Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Long-dated bond yields, however, rose amid ongoing concerns about tighter U.S. monetary policy next year given continued signs of improvement in the U.S. economy. Any rate hike in the U.S. is likely to be followed by Hong Kong due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  link.  \par \par \uc2 The 10-year EF note was quoted at 4.50%, compared with 4.47% Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Lower Hibors also led to a widening in the Hong Kong dollar forward discounts.  \par \par \uc2 The one-year contract was quoted at a discount of 370-350, compared with 330-310 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                   Latest        Late Tuesday \par Overnight Hibor   0.02%           0.02% \par 1-mo Hibor        0.05%           0.10% \par 3-mo Hibor        0.29%           0.30% \par 1-yr Hibor        1.08%           1.10% \par USD/HKD Spot      HK$7.7630       HK$7.7539 \par 6-mo HKD Fwd      -290 to -280    -280 to -265 \par 1-yr HKD Fwd      -370 to -350    -330 to -310 \par  \par 3.73% EF Note Due Jun. 5, 2013: \par  \par    Price: 94.43 Vs 94.63 \par    Yield: 4.50% Vs 4.47% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Raymond Tsoi, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; raymond.tsoi@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by John Viljoen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1053 4178  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031112dzbc000el\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
