\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr weakens after HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2003\par 11:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Nov 12 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar weakened\par on Wednesday after the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought\par another US$100 million against the local unit in an attempt to\par stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after a bout of recent strength.\par     This is the fourth time since late on Monday that the\par territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The HKMA has\par now bought a total of US$300 million this week, according to\par information it publishes daily on Reuters screens .\par     As a result, the HKMA is forecasting the aggregate balance, a\par key measure of interbank liquidity, to rise to HK$6.637 billion\par on Friday.\par     At 0921 GMT, the Hong Kong dollar was trading at 7.7640\par versus the previous close of 7.7585 at 0914 GMT on Tuesday and\par 7.7380 in London trade on Monday.\par     "I think the HKMA, with its presence in the market, is\par showing speculators that it is there to take them on," said a\par dealer from a European bank.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The HKMA is obligated to defend the Hong Kong dollar from\par weakening below its HK$7.80 peg with the U.S. dollar but has no\par mandate to stop it from strengthening above that level.\par  \par     The spot rate (USD/HKD) is expected to move between 7.75-7.77\par in the near term, another dealer said.\par     "It will not rise above 7.77 as that has been a strong\par resistance level lately," said the dealer.\par     Interbank rates and forward rates continued to be weighed\par down by a further expansion in the aggregate balance.\par     The six-month interbank rate fell to 0.40-0.45 percent in the\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 afternoon from the morning's 0.43-0.45 percent. Meanwhile, the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 one-year rate was quoted at 1.02-1.05 percent, compared with   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1.03-1.07 percent in the morning.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The discount on one-year forwards widened to 365/355   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 pips by late afternoon versus 330/310 pips at 0940 GMT on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tuesday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Further downside is expected given abundant liquidity in the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 market with short-term rates near to zero. People need to lend   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 out longer-dated funds. One-year forwards will test early   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October's low of -400 pips and the next target will be -420 to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -450," said a dealer at a French bank.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The market is also looking ahead to U.S. economic data due   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 later this week for hints on the health of the U.S. economy and   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trading clues.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Producer prices, retail sales and industrial production\par figures are due on Friday.\par                      Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0904 GMT   At 0329 GMT   At 0855 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7635/36     7.7599/00     7.7610/20\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -183 / -178   -180 / -172   -175 / -165\par     Six-month        -292 / -282   -290 / -280   -270 / -255\par     One-year         -365 / -355   -360 / -340   -310 / -290\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight        0.01 / 0.02   0.01 / 0.01   0.01 / 0.02\par     Three-month      0.20 / 0.23   0.21 / 0.23   0.20 / 0.23\par     Six-month        0.40 / 0.45   0.43 / 0.45   0.44 / 0.47\par     One-year         1.02 / 1.05   1.03 / 1.07   1.05 / 1.08\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par Reuters contributor page .\par     (US$=HK$7.8).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031112dzbc00220\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
