\par\par \b \uc2 PRESS DIGEST - HONG KONG - Nov 12.  \b0\par\par\uc2 559 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2003\par 02:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong, November 12 (Reuters) - These are some of the leading stories in Hong Kong newspapers on Wednesday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG ECONOMIC TIMES  \par \par \uc2 - China Unicom (0762.HK) will be injected with the assets of nine provincial networks worth 2 billion yuan from its parent firm by the end of this year, according to the state council's asset management branch.  \par \par \uc2 APPLE DAILY  \par \par \uc2 - The government is studying a new proposal to further downsize the civil service by 14,000 job positions in three years. Civil service affairs secretary Joseph Wong said the plan will look at over-staffing in certain job categories and departments.  \par \par \uc2 - The government is said to be prescribing a sharp 30 to 40 percent funding cut to Hong Kong universities over the next three years.  \par \par \uc2 MING PAO DAILY NEWS  \par \par \uc2 - OFTA chief Au Man-ho admits that Hong Kong is two years behind Japan and Korea in mobile data services.  \par \par \uc2 SING TAO DAILY  \par \par \uc2 - Shenzhen ports total cargo handling surpassed for the first time Hong Kong's Kwai Chung ports in October with 5,000 more TEUs to 1.03 million.  \par \par \uc2 - Sino Land has decided to raise the price of flats in its new estate Residence Oasis this week by 3 percent after a brisk four-day internal sale.  \par \par \uc2 SOUTH CHINA MORNING POST  \par \par \uc2 - Securities and Futures Commission chairman Andrew Sheng yesterday rejected claims that a proposal to tighten regulations on listing sponsors was too harsh, saying investment banks had misunderstood the plan.  \par \par \uc2 - British Prime Minister Tony Blair yesterday welcomed the plan by the Hong Kong government to launch a public consultation on constitutional reform next year.  \par \par \uc2 THE STANDARD  \par \par \uc2 - The government will probably complete the securitisation of its toll tunnels and bridge projects to raise HK$6 billion in the current fiscal year, Fitch Ratings said.  \par \par \uc2 - Hong Kong's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has once again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets - selling HK$1.55 billion for US dollars in a bid to stem a sharp spike in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG ECONOMIC JOURNAL  \par \par \uc2 - Hong Kong companies will offer the lowest pay increases among their Asian counterparts next year - from an average of 1.3 to 1.7 percent, according to a survey by consultant firm Hewitt.  \par \par \uc2 - MTRC (0066.HK) denied market rumours saying it has no plans to spin off its 57 percent-owned smart card operator Octopus for a separate public listing.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG DAILY NEWS  \par \par \uc2 - SmarTone (0315.HK) denied a market rumour about the company slashing tariffs by half. It said fee adjustments will be market driven.  \par \par \uc2 SING PAO  \par \par \uc2 - Negative equity mortgages in Hong Kong fell below 100,000 cases in the third quarter, according to the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The decrease was 5.6 percent from the previous quarter.  \par \par \uc2 WEN WEI PO  \par \par \uc2 - Hong Kong stocks fell, dragged by the plunge in the Japan bourse, with the Hang Seng Index below the 12,000 level at one point. It closed just above this level at 12,003, down 153 points on turnover of HK$11.9 billion on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 TA KUNG PAO  \par \par \uc2 - China's second largest insurer Ping An says it plans an IPO share sale in Hong Kong in the first quarter of 2004 to raise a target US$2 billion.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031112dzbc0005u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
