\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr weakens slightly after HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 686 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2003\par 12:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Nov 11 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar\par weakened after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par earlier on Tuesday aimed at stabilising the market after a\par sharp spike in the previous session.\par     Despite the move, dealers predicted more volatility ahead.\par    "After a big correction yesterday, there was some bidding\par for the U.S. dollar when the London market entered. The market\par will move up but there is still resistance," said a dealer from\par a European bank.\par     The Hong Kong dollar was trading at 7.7585 at 0914 GMT\par after hitting a session low of 7.7620, compared to a high of\par one-month high of 7.7380 in London trade on Monday after Hong\par Kong's market close.\par     The HKMA, the city's de-facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , sold HK$775\par million (US$100 million) in local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday morning,\par according to information it publishes daily . It also\par sold HK$775 million (US$100 million) on Monday during London\par trading hours.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The HKMA is obligated to defend the Hong Kong dollar from\par weakening below HK$7.80, but has no mandate to prevent it from\par strengthening above that level.\par     "There has been some selling in the forwards market in the\par last couple of days and then selling of U.S. dollar in the spot\par market in London trade overnight," one trader said.\par  \par     The dollar was seen to have run into strong resistance\par above HK$7.77.\par     "The selling is likely due to the unwinding of long US\par dollar positions and loss-cutting," said the trader.\par     Some traders said that inflows for upcoming initial public\par stock offerings in Hong Kong were behind the local unit's\par recent strength.\par     The Hong Kong dollar strengthened suddenly in late\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September on growing signs of an economic recovery and mounting   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 international political pressure on Beijing to introduce   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 greater flexibility in its exchange rate.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There was speculation that the Hong Kong dollar might move   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in tandem with the yuan, should the latter be revalued. Hong   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kong, a former British colony, has been forging ever closer   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economic ties with mainland China since it reverted to Chinese   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rule in 1997.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beijing has so far resisted revaluation or a widening of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the trading band, saying it must deal with growing unemployment   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and creaky state banks and government-owned firms first. But it   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 says it plans to float the yuan eventually.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The discounts on Hong Kong dollar forwards has been   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 widening since last Friday, but steadied when the spot rate   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 inched up on Tuesday afternoon.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 0940 GMT, the discount on one-year forwards   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 were trading around 330/310 pips, off the morning's low of 360   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 pips. That compared with 255/240 pips at 0951 GMT on Monday and   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 last Thursday's close of 135/120 pips.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the cash market, interbank rates fell across the board   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on the aggregate balance, a key measure of interbank liquidity,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 which is set to increase to HK$5.851 billion on Thursday from   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HK$4.261 billion on Tuesday.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The one-year rate           was quoted at 1.05-1.08 percent\par by late afternoon, down from 1.20-1.25 percent on Monday.\par     "I think the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will remain strong with\par interbank rates continuing in a downward trend," a dealer from\par a Japanese bank said.\par                      Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                       At 0855 GMT   At 0350 GMT   At 0951 GMT\par      HK$ SPOT         7.7610/20     7.7520/23     7.7670/75\par      FORWARDS\par      Three-month      -175 / -165   -183 / -173   -165 / -155\par      Six-month        -270 / -255   -300 / -285   -245 / -235\par      One-year         -310 / -290   -370 / -340   -255 / -240\par      INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par      Overnight        0.01 / 0.02  0.005 / 0.01   0.01 / 0.01\par      Three-month      0.20 / 0.23   0.20 / 0.25   0.30 / 0.32\par      Six-month        0.44 / 0.47   0.43 / 0.47   0.65 / 0.68\par      One-year         1.05 / 1.08   1.10 / 1.13   1.20 / 1.25\par      Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Live quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (US$=HK$7.8).   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031111dzbb0020l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
