\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr weakens after Snow, U.S. GDP report.   \b0\par\par\uc2 777 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2003\par 10:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Oct 31 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar weakened\par against the greenback on Friday, driven by news of surprisingly\par strong U.S. economic growth and after Treasury Secretary John\par Snow's testimony ended without him accusing Japan and China of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manipulation.\par  \par     "Bidding interest emerged for the U.S. dollar in reaction to\par U.S. Treasury report," said a dealer at a local bank.\par     But the dealer added that some profit taking took place when\par the local unit weakened to around 7.7690 in early trade and then\par struggled between 7.7630-50 in the afternoon.\par     At 0912 GMT, the Hong Kong dollar was trading at 7.7660,\par compared with 7.7592 at 0916 GMT on Thursday.\par     It remained above its linked exchange rate of HK$7.80, but is\par expected to creep back towards the peg rate in the near term,\par dealers said.\par     After a sudden strengthening in late September, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar has slowly retreated, aided by several \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from   \f28 \par \par \uc2 the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and repeated statements   \par \par \uc2 from China rebuffing U.S. pressure for a yuan revaluation.   \par \par \uc2 "The U.S. GDP figures were strong and if the unemployment   \par \par \uc2 report shows further improvement next week that may spark an   \par \par \uc2 inflow of funds back to the U.S.," said a dealer from a Japanese   \par \par \uc2 bank.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Commerce Department reported on Thursday that gross   \par \par \uc2 domestic product (GDP) for the third quarter surged 7.2 percent,   \par \par \uc2 its fastest pace in almost 20 years.   \par \par \uc2 A strong recovery in the United States is expected to boost   \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's own. The United States is the territory's second   \par \par \uc2 largest trading partner.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Snow told the U.S. Senate Banking Committee that   \par \par \uc2 the Treasury was actively urging China to end its decade-old   \par \par \uc2 practice of pegging its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at about 8.28 to the U.S.   \par \par \uc2 dollar.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     But he resisted the idea of setting a deadline for China\par because of the effect that would have on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\par     "Upward pressure on Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  alleviated after John\par Snow's soft tone on China," the Japanese bank dealer said.\par     One-year Chinese yuan non-deliverable forwards were dealt at\par 2,850 points on Friday, versus 3,200 points on Thursday.\par     The discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards narrowed on Friday,\par tracking the direction in the spot rate, but some profit taking\par emerged at the high level.\par     One-year forwards          were trading at -115/-110 pips at\par 0930 GMT, versus -95 pips early in the morning and -155/-140 pips\par late on Thursday.\par     In the cash market, Hong Kong interbank rates inched higher\par on the back of firmer forwards rates and U.S. bond yields.\par     The one-year local rate was quoted at 1.25-1.28 percent, up\par from 1.17-1.23 percent on Thursday.\par     The market had little reaction to the government's report\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 that its budget deficit grew to HK$74.3 billion (US$9.5 billion)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 over the six months to end-September, up 23 percent compared with   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the first five months of the fiscal year.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite the sharp increase, most analysts say the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 government's 2003/04 budget deficit target of HK$78 billion - or   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 about six percent of gross domestic product - is still   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 realistic. The majority of its revenues are typically collected   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 towards the end of the fiscal year as tax payments come in.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Dealers said they would keep an eye on U.S. economic data due\par later in the day to see if the U.S. outlook remains bright.\par     The University of Michigan releases the final October\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 consumer sentiment index at 1445 GMT. National Association of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Purchasing Management-Chicago releases October index of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 manufacturing activity at 1500 GMT. Economists polled by Reuters   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expect a rise in the index to 55.5 from 51.2 in September.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0855 GMT   At 0300 GMT   At 0855 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7655/60     7.7646/56     7.7596/98\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -130 / -120   -128 / -120   -140 / -135\par     Six-month        -148 / -138   -145 / -135   -175 / -165\par     One-year         -120 / -110   -110 / - 95   -155 / -140\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight        0.01 / 0.01   0.01 / 0.02   0.01 / 0.02\par     Three-month      0.42 / 0.47   0.42 / 0.45   0.37 / 0.42\par     Six-month        0.75 / 0.80   0.75 / 0.80   0.70 / 0.75\par     One-year         1.25 / 1.28   1.25 / 1.28   1.17 / 1.23\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par Reuters contributor page .\par     (US$=HK$7.8).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2