\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dlr Mkts Late: HK$, Forwards Steady After Yam Remarks  \b0\par\par\uc2 528 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2003\par 10:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong dollar forwards and the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's spot rate were little changed Wednesday as remarks by the city's quasi central banker that he had a "relaxed attitude" about the Hong Kong dollar's recent appreciation had little impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 The USD/HKD spot exchange rate moved a touch lower, to around 7.7440 Wednesday from 7.7480 Tuesday. The benchmark one-year forward contract was also largely unchanged, at a discount of 175 to 165 to the spot rate.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chief Executive Joseph Yam said in a speech late Tuesday: "Our somewhat relaxed attitude toward small deviations in the exchange rate on the strong side of 7.80 does not mean that we are any less committed to maintaining the link."  \par \par \uc2 "It's difficult to pin anything on Yam's speech," a trader said, noting that the USD/HKD spot rate actually went down despite the HKMA's sale of HK$969 million yesterday.  \par \par \uc2 The trader said he didn't expect the USD/HKD rate to rise above 7.75 in the near term, arguing that there are still many market participants long in U.S. dollars who haven't been able to completely liquidate their positions following the recent strengthening of the Hong Kong dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The injection of new liquidity by the HKMA helped depress already low Hong Kong interbank offered rates. The three-month Hibor was quoted at 0.43%, compared with 0.49% Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 With Hong Kong dollar interest rates now, unusually, below their U.S. dollar counterparts, Citigroup economist Joe Lo issued a report predicting they would converge in two to three months.  \par \par \uc2 He estimated that would be the amount of time it would take for excess liquidity to drain out of the system and for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to ease their speculation over an upward revaluation of the Chinese yuan, which is also creating appreciation pressure on the Hong Kong dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The greater liquidity brought on by the HKMA's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also helped prompt more buying interest in short-term \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  Exchange Fund bills by banks. Another trader said the three-month note yield was quoted as low as 0.01%.  \par \par \uc2 There was less activity in longer-dated Exchange Fund notes, though there was some interest in the two-year note, whose yield declined slightly to 1.21%. The yield on the 10-year note rose to 4.47% in response to investors switching out of U.S. Treasurys and into U.S. stocks.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                   Latest        Late Tuesday \par Overnight Hibor   0.03%         0.04% \par 1-mo Hibor        0.14%         0.32% \par 3-mo Hibor        0.43%         0.49% \par 1-yr Hibor        1.07%         1.10% \par USD/HKD Spot      HK$7.7440     HK$7.7480 \par 6-mo HKD Fwd      -190 to -175  -160 to -140 \par 1-yr HKD Fwd      -175 to -165  -180 to -160 \par  \par 3.73% EF Note Due June 5, 2013: \par  \par    Price: 94.60 Vs 94.68 \par    Yield: 4.47% Vs 4.46% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Andrew Batson, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; andrew.batson@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by John Viljoen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1053 4178  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031015dzaf000hk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
