\par\par \b \uc2 PRESS DIGEST - HONG KONG - Oct 15.  \b0\par\par\uc2 548 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2003\par 02:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong, Oct 15 (Reuters) - These are some of the leading stories in Hong Kong newspapers on Wednesday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG ECONOMIC TIMES  \par \par \uc2 - Sources say Hong Kong-based Cathay Pacific Airways (0293.HK) has received approval from mainland aviation authorities to start operating flights to Beijing from early December.  \par \par \uc2 APPLE DAILY  \par \par \uc2 - Li Ka-shing controlled Cheung Kong Holdings (0001.HK) announced the start of its HK$10 billion retail bond programme yesterday with the first batch worth HK$800 million for subscription starting today. There are Hong Kong and Australian dollar tranches and the minimum subscription is HK$50,000 and A$10,000.  \par \par \uc2 - The Hong Kong government's trustworthiness fell to a record low of only 25 percent in the latest opinion poll conducted by the University of Hong Kong.  \par \par \uc2 MING PAO DAILY NEWS  \par \par \uc2 - Hong Kong stocks' day-high of 12,065 points yesterday moved the index to a record high for the last 26 months. But it failed to stand at that level with the index erasing the gain and falling over 100 points to close at 11,856.  \par \par \uc2 - A spokesman for the Rolling Stones said the rock band has a contract, suggesting they will play in the Hong Kong Harbour Fest in November despite earlier reports they had withdrawn from the show.  \par \par \uc2 SING TAO DAILY  \par \par \uc2 - Hongkong Land (HKLD.SI), the largest private landlord in Hong Kong, will return to the local residential flat market after a 20 year absence with the launch of a new estate in Western next month.  \par \par \uc2 - The Hospital Authority has decided to release its review report on the SARS epidemic in full on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 SOUTH CHINA MORNING POST  \par \par \uc2 - Mainland firms that fail to meet listing requirements at home are turning to the Growth Enterprise Market, where rules for IPOs are considered less stringent.  \par \par \uc2 - Crime syndicates behind a wave of mortgage scams are targeting new estates, hoping to snap up the sweetest mortgage deals - and attract tenants to further boost their profits, which police say can be as high as 12 percent of the flat value.  \par \par \uc2 THE STANDARD  \par \par \uc2 - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the fourth time in the past two weeks yesterday, pumping HK$969 million into it in a bid to stem the local dollars' continued strength against the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 - Analysts expect New World Development's full-year net profit to plunge by an average 78 percent due to the absence of a one-off gain in the previous year.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG ECONOMIC JOURNAL  \par \par \uc2 - Details of more property market-saving measures will be announced today. The government has decided not to take back the rights to develop sites along MTR and KCRC train lines, but it is demanding that rail companies supply no new flats before 2008.  \par \par \uc2 - Friday marks the 20th anniversary of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to the US dollar. \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief executive Joseph Yam says Hong Kong does not need to make any changes to the peg.  \par \par \uc2 WEN WEI PO  \par \par \uc2 - China will send its first man into space this morning with the launch of the Shenzhou V spacecraft. Yang Liwei was chosen for the mission. President Hu Jintao has arrived at the launch site.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031015dzaf00090\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscale