\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dlr Mkts Late: HK$ Dn As HKMA Move Has Mixed Results  \b0\par\par\uc2 508 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2003\par 10:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar weakened Tuesday, although an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to damp its recent appreciation had mixed results.  \par \par \uc2 Late Tuesday, the U.S. dollar was quoted around HK$7.7500, near the level at which traders said the HKMA had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars and buy U.S. dollars. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar actually strengthened somewhat immediately after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but later sank again against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The result (of the HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) wasn't ideal," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards narrowed in line with the discount on yuan non-deliverable forwards, traders said. The one-year Hong Kong dollar forward was quoted at a discount of 180 to 160 to the spot rate, compared with a discount of 250 to 230 Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said position adjustment ahead of the Asia Pacific Economic Cooperation forum summit narrowed the yuan non-deliverable forwards discount, which pushed Hong Kong dollar forwards higher.  \par \par \uc2 "The tightening of the one-year yuan NDF discount back to below the 4000 key level spurred waves of profit-taking in Hong Kong dollar forwards," a trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Traders, however, expect further upside for forwards to be firmly capped given the excess liquidity in the interbank market after recent equity-driven inflows and injections from the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong interbank offered rates rose as the Hong Kong dollar weakened, The one-month Hibor was quoted at 0.32%, compared with 0.21% Monday. However, the overnight Hibor fell to 0.04% because of the HKMA's injection of liquidity through its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  Exchange Fund note yields rose marginally as recent strength in local shares continued to spur funds to switch into equities and out of bonds.  \par \par \uc2 The two-year EF note was quoted at 1.21%, compared with 1.17% Monday. The 10-year EF note was quoted at 4.46%, up from 4.40% previously.  \par \par \uc2 "If the Hang Seng Index stays firmly above 12,000 points, we may see more switching into shares and therefore a continued upward bias of bond yields," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's blue-chip Hang Seng index closed down 0.9% Tuesday at 11856.  \par \par \uc2 Higher Hong Kong dollar forwards also added to the selling pressure on bonds, traders added.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                   Latest        Late Monday \par Overnight Hibor    0.04%          0.05% \par 1-mo Hibor         0.32%          0.21% \par 3-mo Hibor         0.49%          0.41% \par 1-yr Hibor         1.10%          1.02% \par USD/HKD Spot       HK$7.7480      HK$7.7340 \par 6-mo HKD Fwd       -160 to -140   -210 to -200 \par 1-yr HKD Fwd       -160 to -120   -250 to -230 \par  \par 3.73% EF Note Due June 5, 2013: \par  \par    Price: 94.68 Vs 95.13 \par    Yield: 4.46% Vs 4.40% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Raymond Tsoi and Andrew Batson, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; andrew.batson@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by John Viljoen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1053 4178  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031014dzae000cm\par