\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA's Yam: Will  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  To Maintain Confidence In Peg  \b0\par\par\uc2 479 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2003\par 10:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's quasi \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if it is necessary to maintain the confidence of the markets and the public in the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar, Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief executive Joseph Yam said Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "Our responsibility is to maintain the stability of the exchange rate and observe the sentiment of the market. We will act accordingly and respond to the market sentiment," he told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 "We can't tolerate any deviation which is big enough to undermine confidence in the system. Then we will respond to the market," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Yam wouldn't discuss any specific \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar market, including today's when the HKMA sold HK$969 million, or indicate a specific level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it would try to defend.  \par \par \uc2 The peg system has come under an unusual challenge recently, as the Hong Kong dollar has spent weeks trading above its pegged rate of 7.80 to the U.S. dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system has an automatic mechanism to prevent devaluation, but any move to prevent appreciation must be through discretionary sales, or \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , by the HKMA.  \par \par \uc2 That recent deviation from the pegged rate has caused some questioning of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, though officials have reiterated that there has been no actual change in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, only a change in market sentiment.  \par \par \uc2 Asked repeatedly about the HKMA's plans for \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bring the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to its 7.80 peg, Yam emphasized that its actions wouldn't be driven by specific numerical targets, but by the desire to maintain overall confidence in the peg.  \par \par \uc2 "It all depends on the market sentiment. If they are comfortable and are not questioning the credibility of the system, then we will leave the market to work it out," Yam said.  \par \par \uc2 Yam's remarks came at a briefing on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to mark its twentieth anniversary, which falls on Friday. He also repeated the HKMA's standard insistence that it has no intention of abandoning the linked exchange rate system.  \par \par \uc2 "We surely need it," he said. "For the past 20 years, the system has made a great contribution to Hong Kong's stability and prosperity. In a market where there is free flow of capital, an exchange rate peg will help businesses to defend against volatility."  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA acts as Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it isn't an independent one. Yam noted that he and the HKMA report to Financial Secretary Henry Tang, who would be the one who would make any policy decision to continue, change or abandon the peg system.  \par \par \uc2 -By Andrew Batson and Loretta Ng, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; andrew.batson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by John Viljoen  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031014dzae000bw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
