\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 Interveness \highlight\uc2  In HK Dollar Mkt, Sells HK$969 Million  \b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2003\par 09:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying U.S. dollars and selling Hong Kong dollars in an attempt to bring the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closer to its peg rate of 7.80.  \par \par \uc2 "The result wasn't ideal. The rate actually went down," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said, noting that the HKMA's sales were made when the U.S. dollar/HK dollar spot rate was at around 7.75, but that it had actually declined after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was quoted at around HK$7.7480 at 0745 GMT. Since Sept. 22, the Hong Kong dollar has been trading above its pegged rate of 7.80 to the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The sales were made in two separate transactions about ten to fifteen minutes apart, the trader said. They totaled HK$969 million, according to HKMA data distributed to financial information terminals.  \par \par \uc2 It wasn't immediately clear what triggered the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the HKMA normally doesn't comment on its market activities.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA's previous \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , during the past weeks when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar has been stronger than the peg rate, have been at around 7.70 or 7.73, higher than the today's level.  \par \par \uc2 Traders have also said that volatility in the Hong Kong dollar market had been easing in recent days, with most expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilize and trade within a tight range of 7.72 to 7.74 in coming weeks.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA, which acts as Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is obliged to buy the Hong Kong dollar from banks at the peg rate, which essentially puts a floor on the Hong Kong dollar's level against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 However, the convertibility undertaking is one-sided, which means that selling the Hong Kong dollar is at the HKMA's discretion. Therefore there is theoretically no ceiling for the Hong Kong dollar's value.  \par \par \uc2 -By Andrew Batson, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; andrew.batson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031014dzae000a4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
