\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  again on dollar.   \b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2003\par 10:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oct 14 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought US$125 million and sold HK$969 million on Tuesday afternoon - the sixth time in less than four weeks that the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped into the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since the local dollar suddenly climbed.    \par \par \uc2  "The figure reflected banks selling U.S. dollars to us. We have been selling Hong Kong dollars. Banks approached us to do it," the spokesman told Reuters. The spot rate briefly weakened to HK$7.75 to the U.S. dollar after the injection but then firmed back to HK$7.7464 as of 0738 GMT, and remained well below the local dollar's official pegged exchange rate of 7.8 to the U.S. dollar.    \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar shot up to HK$7.7050 in late September, its strongest level since the Asian financial crisis of 1997-98, on growing signs that its long ailing economy was recovering.    \par \par \uc2  Mounting international pressure on Beijing to revalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also fuelled expectations that Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will icreasingly move in tune with China's as the two economies become more closely integrated.    \par \par \uc2  Despite repeated HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has remained stubbornly strong, though many dealers expect it will slowly drift back to the pegged level over time.    \par \par \uc2  The HKMA has repeatedly said it remained committed to maintaining the 20-year-old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, which has often been described as a pillar of the former British colony's economy.    \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar moved up last month after a statement from the G7 industrial nations meeting urging exchange rate flexibility.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031014dzae000zj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
