\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr weakens in afternoon trade on profit taking.   \b0\par\par\uc2 715 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2003\par 12:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Oct 8 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar weakened\par sharply on Wednesday afternoon, heading back towards its pegged\par exchange rate to the U.S. dollar, as some dealers took profits\par after a highly unusual strengthening two weeks ago.\par     The local unit was trading at HK$7.7427/37 per U.S. dollar at\par 5.39 p.m. (0939 GMT) compared to the morning's HK$7.7124 level,\par but remained well above its HK$7.80 pegged exchange rate.\par     Four \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last\par week and fears of more by the de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stabilise\par the spot rate may have convinced some traders to sqaure Hong Kong\par dollar positions.\par     Many traders had expected its rare show of strength to be\par short-lived. Although the territory's economy is showing signs of\par picking up, the rebound has been patchy.\par     "This move could just be profit taking by some people who had\par long Hong Kong dollar positions at the HK$7.78 level.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  After it\par strengthened to around HK$7.71, they may have decided to just\par take profits," said Eddie Wong, chief strategist for Asia at ABN\par AMRO.\par     The Hong Kong dollar climbed to HK$7.7020 last Friday, its\par strongest level since the 1997/98 Asian financial crisis,\par triggered by a call by industrialised countries for more flexible\par exchange rates, strong fund inflows into the surging stock market\par  and by hopes that the long ailing economy was in a sustainable\par recovery.\par     The discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards sharply narrowed on\par Wednesday afternoon, suggesting that investors are betting that\par the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will not appreciate by as much as they were\par expecting it to earlier in the day.\par  \par     The one-year Hong Kong dollar forwards narrowed to -180/-160\par late on Wednesday from -410/-395 late on Tuesday.\par     "There was some outright purchases from fund houses in the\par spot and forwards markets," one trader said.\par     "Some investors booked profits after the one-year forwards\par fell to a discount of -400. A narrowing in discount of yuan NDFs\par also helped the market," the dealer added.\par      Hong Kong dollar forwards had been moving toward a discount\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 when the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suddenly rose on September 22, after a   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 statement from the Group of Seven industrial nations urging   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 exchange rate flexibility.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Forwards fell into a deeper discount early on Tuesday in   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 tandem with yuan NDFs on persistent speculation of a revaluation   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of the Chinese yuan.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Market jitters alleviated as Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao said   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China would keep its yuan exchange rate stable," another dealer   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from a European bank said.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     One-year yuan NDFs           were dealt at -4,500 points\par compared with -5,300 points late on Tuesday.\par     China manages the yuan in a 8.27-8.28 per dollar range, which\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 other countries have criticised as too weak, saying it gives   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China an unfair trade advantage. Hong Kong's economy is   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 increasingly integrated with mainland China's.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers said speculation on a move in the yuan has   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 intensified ahead of the APEC leaders summit in Bangkok later   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 this month, in which the region's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies, especially   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 those of China, are expected to be raised.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The sharp correction in the spot and forwards markets pushed\par up interbank rates.\par     The three- and six-month interbank rates were bid at 0.37 and\par 0.50 percent respectively in late afternoon, compared with 0.21\par and 0.33 percent in the morning.\par                      Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0933 GMT   At 0400 GMT   At 0925 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7450/53     7.7130/40     7.7097/100\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -110 / -100   -165 / -155   -185 / -165\par     Six-month        -170 / -150   -270 / -260   -320 / -300\par     One-year         -180 / -150   -375 / -355   -410 / -395\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight        0.03 / 0.09   0.05 / 0.06   0.12 / 0.18\par     Three-month      0.50 / 0.56   0.18 / 0.21   0.18 / 0.25\par     Six-month        0.62 / 0.72   0.31 / 0.33   0.37 / 0.43\par     One-year         1.00 / 1.06   0.73 / 0.75   0.72 / 0.75\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par Reuters contributor page .\par     (US$=HK$7.8).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031008dza80020p\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\